WEBVTT


00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.100
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.725
And some hamachi. Two pieces.


00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.433
What is a "holiday roll"?


00:03:42.058 --> 00:03:43.058
Okay.


00:03:43.808 --> 00:03:44.892
Thank you.


00:03:49.017 --> 00:03:50.933
I'm late, I know. Sorry.


00:03:52.017 --> 00:03:53.642
They kept me at work an extra hour.


00:03:54.058 --> 00:03:54.892
Are you okay?


00:03:55.225 --> 00:03:55.975
Okay.


00:03:56.558 --> 00:03:57.600
What's that?


00:03:57.933 --> 00:03:59.142
I fell off my bike.


00:03:59.725 --> 00:04:01.142
- That thing?
- Yeah.


00:04:02.142 --> 00:04:03.517
Looks like you never rode it.


00:04:03.725 --> 00:04:04.725
And you see why?


00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:10.142
You've carefully avoided saying what this job is.


00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:13.183
I told you, it's entry level.


00:04:13.683 --> 00:04:16.308
But there's a fast track to promotion.


00:04:16.475 --> 00:04:17.433
Kind of manager.


00:04:17.642 --> 00:04:19.100
Kind of McDonald's?


00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:20.433
Yeah.


00:04:21.725 --> 00:04:24.225
I brought you a present.


00:04:25.517 --> 00:04:26.850
It's from Josie, really.


00:04:27.683 --> 00:04:28.975
It was her idea.


00:04:30.517 --> 00:04:31.850
You look very handsome.


00:04:33.933 --> 00:04:36.892
We'll go back and take another photo after the birth.


00:04:37.183 --> 00:04:38.642
Like a before and after.


00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.267
Josie's full of ideas for decorating.


00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.558
She never had her own place till now.


00:04:45.308 --> 00:04:47.517
How much do you need for the apartment?


00:04:50.183 --> 00:04:50.933
I didn't ask for money.


00:04:51.017 --> 00:04:53.017
No, it was me, hearing voices.


00:04:53.475 --> 00:04:56.683
I planned to ask you to provide collateral, not money.


00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.517
And Josie's boyfriends?


00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.350
Any of them moving in, too?


00:05:03.433 --> 00:05:04.975
No, why...


00:05:05.725 --> 00:05:07.767
Shit! It was just cleaned.


00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:15.683
That girl is clearly dysfunctional.


00:05:15.808 --> 00:05:17.267
You know nothing about her.


00:05:18.475 --> 00:05:21.725
Except she was raised in a commune by unwashed idiots.


00:05:21.808 --> 00:05:23.100
An arts collective.


00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:25.683
Why you? What's she after?


00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:28.308
What could she be after? I have no money.


00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.308
I have.


00:05:30.475 --> 00:05:31.975
What's with you today?


00:05:39.308 --> 00:05:43.225
I'll give you 3 months' rent.
But I look at the place first.


00:05:43.433 --> 00:05:45.225
I didn't want to pressure you.


00:05:45.308 --> 00:05:47.558
You won. Quit while you're ahead.


00:05:58.017 --> 00:05:59.642
- Bye.
- Bye.


00:07:02.183 --> 00:07:04.892
Change all the locks, upstairs and down.


00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:06.475
Okay.


00:07:07.142 --> 00:07:09.225
I left the key in the mailbox.


00:07:09.308 --> 00:07:10.975
Thanks a lot.


00:07:11.225 --> 00:07:13.142
You've seen Vincent's apartment?


00:07:13.225 --> 00:07:15.975
6 months ago, he was dealing weed
and getting into fights.


00:07:16.058 --> 00:07:17.475
You see him as a family man?


00:07:17.683 --> 00:07:20.267
That bitch Josie is a real menace.


00:07:20.975 --> 00:07:23.100
He just doesn't see it.


00:07:54.892 --> 00:07:56.350
Kwan, we agreed


00:07:56.433 --> 00:07:59.058
the orgasmic convulsions are way too timid.


00:07:59.225 --> 00:08:00.933
As if they're scared of sex.


00:08:01.017 --> 00:08:02.600
I upped it 5 times.


00:08:02.683 --> 00:08:04.267
You can't tell. Push it.


00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.142
Can we discuss the real issues?


00:08:07.558 --> 00:08:10.058
We get one shot at Activision,


00:08:10.267 --> 00:08:12.183
but our controller is so crappy


00:08:12.267 --> 00:08:15.142
the demo is almost unplayable.


00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:20.392
What's the point coming up with
hyper realistic environments for Stix


00:08:20.475 --> 00:08:23.267
if the player throws the controller
through the screen!


00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:26.725
Kurt, you're off track,
focusing on known glitches.


00:08:26.808 --> 00:08:27.475
No.


00:08:28.558 --> 00:08:30.183
The real problem is right there.


00:08:31.767 --> 00:08:36.058
The real problem is, your background
in publishing and literature


00:08:36.142 --> 00:08:40.267
is completely inappropriate for
evaluating playability.


00:08:44.683 --> 00:08:49.642
Okay, maybe Anna and I should've
founded a different sort of company.


00:08:49.892 --> 00:08:52.433
Maybe Kronos was only a hit


00:08:52.517 --> 00:08:54.558
thanks to your genius ideas.


00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:58.517
Maybe we're just two bitches who got lucky.


00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.683
But the fact is,


00:08:59.767 --> 00:09:02.308
the boss here is me.


00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:04.933
And we're 6 months behind.


00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:12.933
Our goal is simple, as you all know.


00:09:13.017 --> 00:09:14.600
When the player guts an orc,


00:09:14.683 --> 00:09:17.183
he needs to feel the blood on his hands.


00:09:17.475 --> 00:09:18.975
Thick, warm blood.


00:09:19.183 --> 00:09:20.475
If at all possible.


00:09:20.558 --> 00:09:21.767
Let's go.


00:09:22.767 --> 00:09:24.058
I love you.


00:09:29.433 --> 00:09:32.142
Does Kurt hate me or is it just me?


00:09:32.267 --> 00:09:34.225
No, he hates you.


00:09:34.683 --> 00:09:36.642
They all hate you, except Kevin.


00:09:36.725 --> 00:09:39.725
He really loves you. even if he tries to laugh it off.


00:09:41.975 --> 00:09:43.767
And you knew it, right?


00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:54.517
Press here.


00:09:54.683 --> 00:09:56.683
She knows I want a full STD panel?


00:09:56.767 --> 00:09:57.933
Yes, of course.


00:09:58.142 --> 00:10:01.267
If you're worried about a recent exposure,


00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:02.975
I can prescribe a PEP.


00:10:03.433 --> 00:10:06.308
No, I looked online. Too many side effects.


00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:08.975
I can't miss any work.


00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.767
I guess we roll the dice.


00:10:34.475 --> 00:10:35.267
Hello?


00:10:35.725 --> 00:10:37.683
My evening just cleared up.


00:10:38.892 --> 00:10:40.892
- I can't.
- Make an effort.


00:10:40.975 --> 00:10:43.350
I can't. I have...


00:10:44.558 --> 00:10:47.183
I have my period. I'm not well.


00:10:47.725 --> 00:10:49.475
I'll wear a condom.


00:10:50.642 --> 00:10:52.350
I appreciate your sense of sacrifice.


00:10:52.433 --> 00:10:54.642
A little blood doesn't turn me off.


00:10:54.767 --> 00:10:55.933
No, I can't.


00:10:56.225 --> 00:10:57.183
See you.


00:11:04.558 --> 00:11:07.642
Scum!


00:11:41.933 --> 00:11:43.308
You and your father.


00:11:43.517 --> 00:11:44.975
I love everything you do to me.


00:11:45.475 --> 00:11:48.433
Let's do it again.


00:11:52.433 --> 00:11:54.058
Next time, ring the bell.


00:11:54.433 --> 00:11:57.850
If you want to avoid being treated to upsetting sights,


00:11:57.933 --> 00:12:01.142
Then you won't be treated to gruesome sights.


00:12:01.433 --> 00:12:03.350
I'd better put some pants on.


00:12:05.767 --> 00:12:07.225
How much do you pay them?


00:12:07.433 --> 00:12:09.725
-It's pitiful! -Save your pity.


00:12:09.808 --> 00:12:11.225
I'm not ashamed.


00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.350
It's my life. My sex life.


00:12:13.433 --> 00:12:14.975
You're a little bitch, Michèle.


00:12:15.058 --> 00:12:17.767
I'm just saying, with your finances. be careful.


00:12:17.892 --> 00:12:19.558
Did you eat? I made spaghetti.


00:12:19.642 --> 00:12:21.017
I'll take a coffee.


00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:23.183
- Not taking your coat off?
- I'm cold.


00:12:26.517 --> 00:12:28.267
You had more work done?


00:12:28.475 --> 00:12:30.058
Will you stop going on about that?


00:12:31.433 --> 00:12:32.892
I'm sorry.


00:12:32.975 --> 00:12:35.058
Just a little Botox.


00:12:35.308 --> 00:12:36.683
It's your business.


00:12:40.308 --> 00:12:40.892
Very good.


00:12:40.975 --> 00:12:42.267
You seem surprised.


00:12:42.433 --> 00:12:43.767
Better like this?


00:12:44.558 --> 00:12:47.100
Michèle, some other time, I have to take off.


00:12:47.308 --> 00:12:48.683
No. not yet.


00:12:54.392 --> 00:12:56.600
My mother told you she's HIV-positive?


00:12:56.767 --> 00:12:59.183
I warned Ralf you'd try that one.


00:12:59.475 --> 00:13:00.975
Nice meeting you.


00:13:06.267 --> 00:13:08.433
One question. Think before you answer.


00:13:08.683 --> 00:13:10.892
What would you say if I remarried?


00:13:10.975 --> 00:13:12.600
It's simple, I'd kill you.


00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.142
No need to think.


00:13:14.433 --> 00:13:17.475
You always wanted a sanitized version of life.


00:13:17.558 --> 00:13:19.142
You asked, I answered.


00:13:19.433 --> 00:13:20.517
I'd kill you.


00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:23.558
You're so selfish, it's frightening.


00:13:24.058 --> 00:13:25.058
I know.


00:13:28.017 --> 00:13:29.850
By the way, here's your check.


00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.225
You never give anything truly of yourself.


00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:38.600
- Your father, it's such an ordeal?
- Don't.


00:13:38.683 --> 00:13:40.725
- He's old.
- Still breathing.


00:13:40.808 --> 00:13:42.308
Some bonds never break.


00:13:42.392 --> 00:13:44.558
I walk in and it's one horror after another.


00:13:44.642 --> 00:13:46.267
He has a parole hearing.


00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:48.600
That's enough. Okay?


00:13:52.725 --> 00:13:55.017
Your stud forgot his hernia belt.


00:14:02.267 --> 00:14:04.392
- You need a hand?
- No, I've got it.


00:14:06.767 --> 00:14:08.183
Is it big enough?


00:14:08.725 --> 00:14:11.267
Any taller and the star will scrape the ceiling.


00:14:14.517 --> 00:14:15.517
Michèle!


00:14:16.225 --> 00:14:16.892
Evening.


00:14:16.975 --> 00:14:19.517
I'm so glad I caught you. Here...


00:14:19.892 --> 00:14:21.392
I'm handing these out.


00:14:21.517 --> 00:14:24.392
It's about the Board's trash separation policy.


00:14:24.475 --> 00:14:25.308
Thank you.


00:14:25.392 --> 00:14:28.350
The fines for non-compliance are exorbitant.


00:14:28.433 --> 00:14:30.642
We're meeting Wednesday to oppose it.


00:14:30.725 --> 00:14:32.808
You're on the Board, aren't you?


00:14:32.892 --> 00:14:35.100
- Yes.
- I've tried to point out


00:14:35.267 --> 00:14:37.267
that minor conflict of interest.


00:14:37.892 --> 00:14:39.600
It's an interesting position.


00:14:39.767 --> 00:14:41.558
Yes, that's right. Exactly.


00:14:42.225 --> 00:14:43.850
I hope you can make it.


00:14:43.975 --> 00:14:45.058
Perhaps.


00:14:45.225 --> 00:14:46.517
-Goodnight. -Goodnight.


00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:50.183
I'll just deliver these.


00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.433
Be right back!


00:15:07.767 --> 00:15:09.058
- Good evening.
- Good evening.


00:15:09.392 --> 00:15:12.725
Last one. Your new keys are on the table.


00:15:12.892 --> 00:15:13.975
Thank you.


00:15:15.433 --> 00:15:17.892
Did you notice the back door jams?


00:15:18.975 --> 00:15:21.433
I only do locks.


00:15:22.308 --> 00:15:24.433
How come?


00:15:24.517 --> 00:15:25.475
Okay.


00:15:53.933 --> 00:15:55.350
How'd you get out there?


00:15:58.058 --> 00:15:59.183
Come on in.


00:16:55.475 --> 00:16:58.892
You didn't have to claw his eyes out but scratch him at least.


00:16:59.058 --> 00:17:00.808
I'm just saying.


00:17:17.925 --> 00:17:19.925
I found you very narrow, for a woman of your age


00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.050
That one's 25.


00:17:33.592 --> 00:17:35.217
That's the Safety Angel.


00:17:35.383 --> 00:17:37.258
- The most powerful?
- Serious stuff.


00:17:37.425 --> 00:17:40.050
0.2 oz of pepper spray at 110 mph.


00:17:40.217 --> 00:17:42.008
Gives you quite an advantage.


00:17:42.633 --> 00:17:43.633
I'll take it.


00:17:53.925 --> 00:17:55.217
And this.


00:18:35.008 --> 00:18:36.050
Hey, you!


00:18:37.633 --> 00:18:39.467
You told Vincent you'd pay his rent?


00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.800
No, I said I'd help out for a while.


00:18:41.967 --> 00:18:44.008
Mr. Casamayou, your table's ready.


00:18:44.675 --> 00:18:47.967
Don't expect me to pitch in. I'm stone broke.


00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:49.675
I'm the one who made the promise.


00:18:50.092 --> 00:18:51.425
Why?


00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:53.967
Struggling to get by builds character.


00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:55.592
Trouble is, he's dating a psycho.


00:18:55.675 --> 00:18:57.092
Thank you very much.


00:18:57.383 --> 00:19:00.425
The wacko won't tolerate struggling.


00:19:00.508 --> 00:19:01.883
Psycho's the word.


00:19:01.967 --> 00:19:04.633
Often though, that kind of girl's good in bed.


00:19:04.967 --> 00:19:07.008
What does that even mean, "good in bed"?


00:19:07.967 --> 00:19:10.383
- I never knew.
- You read my proposal?


00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:17.675
Richard, would you say I'm tight for a woman my age?


00:19:19.092 --> 00:19:20.217
Hi there!


00:19:20.842 --> 00:19:23.425
- Hi.
- Thanks.


00:19:23.633 --> 00:19:25.008
What's up, loser?


00:19:25.092 --> 00:19:26.258
How are you, pumpkin?


00:19:26.342 --> 00:19:30.342
Just in time to hear Michèle avoid giving her thoughts on my game idea.


00:19:30.425 --> 00:19:31.842
No! It was very interesting.


00:19:31.925 --> 00:19:33.425
You bet it's interesting.


00:19:33.508 --> 00:19:35.342
Tell all.


00:19:35.842 --> 00:19:37.217
- Bubbly, 4 glasses.
- No. a bottle!


00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:40.967
It's set in a time when dogs have been wiped out by a virus.


00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:43.925
So people have robotic canines as pets.


00:19:44.092 --> 00:19:46.467
The player's the Spartacus of the robot-dog world.


00:19:47.842 --> 00:19:48.758
Original.


00:19:53.633 --> 00:19:54.842
Interesting.


00:19:55.508 --> 00:19:57.175
I have something to tell you all.


00:20:00.633 --> 00:20:05.133
I was looking for a way of simply and naturally


00:20:05.217 --> 00:20:07.717
tossing this out. but I can't find one.


00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:10.217
So...


00:20:11.133 --> 00:20:13.092
Here goes. I was assaulted...


00:20:13.258 --> 00:20:14.633
...at home.


00:20:16.633 --> 00:20:18.342
I guess I was raped.


00:20:20.675 --> 00:20:21.633
Raped?


00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:24.758
- Oh, my god.
- For real?


00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:26.800
When?


00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:29.425
Thursday, at 3pm.


00:20:29.883 --> 00:20:30.967
And you never said?


00:20:31.508 --> 00:20:34.550
I don't know what to say. What can I say?


00:20:34.842 --> 00:20:36.383
Oh, my god!


00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:40.008
- I feel stupid for bringing it up.
- Are you insane?


00:20:40.925 --> 00:20:42.800
A Piper-Heidsieck.


00:20:43.342 --> 00:20:44.175
Very good.


00:20:45.675 --> 00:20:47.925
Wait a few minutes before popping it.


00:20:51.258 --> 00:20:52.800
Are you alright?


00:20:53.342 --> 00:20:54.675
You have to see a doctor.


00:20:54.925 --> 00:20:56.092
Done that.


00:20:56.217 --> 00:20:57.967
What did the cops say?


00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:01.508
You didn't report it?


00:21:02.217 --> 00:21:04.842
Michèle, you have to report it immediately.


00:21:04.925 --> 00:21:05.842
What for?


00:21:06.217 --> 00:21:07.383
What for!


00:21:07.592 --> 00:21:10.133
It's over. It doesn't need talking about anymore.


00:21:10.717 --> 00:21:12.258
It's not worth a debate.


00:21:16.925 --> 00:21:18.508
How about we order?


00:21:21.425 --> 00:21:22.717
You avoid the police because...


00:21:22.758 --> 00:21:25.050
Of course I avoid the police "because!"


00:21:25.133 --> 00:21:27.717
I won't deal with the police ever again.


00:21:28.008 --> 00:21:30.050
- See you!
- See you!


00:21:30.425 --> 00:21:33.550
- I'll get you a gun.
- A gun! You're out of your mind.


00:21:33.883 --> 00:21:35.342
Richard. I should tell you...


00:21:35.508 --> 00:21:38.633
Your proposal, our investors aren't interested.


00:21:38.717 --> 00:21:40.258
I don't want to discuss it now.


00:21:40.717 --> 00:21:42.633
But I'd like your opinion on it.


00:21:42.717 --> 00:21:45.675
It's got nothing to do with the quality of your work.


00:21:45.925 --> 00:21:50.050
It's a business that's tied into a particular demographic.


00:21:50.133 --> 00:21:52.425
A demographic oblivious to quality?


00:21:52.508 --> 00:21:53.800
Exactly.


00:21:53.883 --> 00:21:55.508
Come on, I can take it!


00:21:55.592 --> 00:21:57.467
Be honest. What did you think of it?


00:21:57.633 --> 00:22:00.925
Richard, go back to your novel. You're a writer.


00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:02.758
Sure. A penniless writer.


00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:06.800
Somebody trashed your fender.


00:22:09.008 --> 00:22:09.967
Somebody?


00:22:12.425 --> 00:22:13.717
See you.


00:22:25.508 --> 00:22:26.675
Shit!


00:22:30.675 --> 00:22:31.925
Here you go.


00:22:36.967 --> 00:22:38.800
I'll be right there, I...


00:22:38.967 --> 00:22:41.050
I'll just grab my jacket.


00:22:45.217 --> 00:22:46.842
You got my sundae?


00:22:49.175 --> 00:22:50.883
Thanks. See you tomorrow.


00:23:02.217 --> 00:23:03.300
Here, for you.


00:23:03.383 --> 00:23:05.383
- For me?
- Yes, made it myself.


00:23:05.467 --> 00:23:07.217
That's so sweet.


00:23:16.175 --> 00:23:18.258
- Delicious.
- Not bad, right?


00:23:21.758 --> 00:23:23.300
Mrs. Leblanc? Hello.


00:23:23.383 --> 00:23:23.842
Hello


00:23:23.925 --> 00:23:26.092
I'm Philippe, from the agency.


00:23:26.175 --> 00:23:28.467
Vincent, good timing, I need you here.


00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:29.883
Hey, Michèle.


00:23:29.925 --> 00:23:32.175
-What can I do? -Stand against the wall.


00:23:32.258 --> 00:23:33.800
- Yeah?
- Yeah.


00:23:34.467 --> 00:23:35.675
With your arms...


00:23:35.842 --> 00:23:39.925
The bookcase is 5 feet wide. I want to visualize it.


00:23:40.092 --> 00:23:41.467
Like this, okay?


00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:42.550
Vincent...


00:23:42.592 --> 00:23:46.050
Don't act the bookcase. Be the bookcase.


00:23:48.258 --> 00:23:49.508
Okay, hold this.


00:23:50.467 --> 00:23:53.008
Vincent is quite the actor.


00:23:54.050 --> 00:23:54.967
Are you hurt?


00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:56.467
- No.
- No, it's fine.


00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:59.967
Age 12, he was young Achilles in Kronos.


00:24:00.133 --> 00:24:01.842
A video game I produced.


00:24:01.925 --> 00:24:03.217
Yeah?


00:24:03.758 --> 00:24:05.925
I bet you were the cutest knight in armor.


00:24:06.008 --> 00:24:07.550
Not too shabby.


00:24:17.008 --> 00:24:18.592
Nice, huh?


00:24:18.967 --> 00:24:21.050
A little too nice, don't you think?


00:24:21.133 --> 00:24:24.092
There's room for a 50-inch here.


00:24:24.175 --> 00:24:25.508
Did you ask her?


00:24:26.842 --> 00:24:28.967
You mentioned a microwave,


00:24:29.050 --> 00:24:33.050
but we thought a TV makes a better housewarming present.


00:24:33.342 --> 00:24:35.967
Don't you need an oven more than a TV?


00:24:36.050 --> 00:24:39.008
We don't need one. The kitchen comes fully equipped.


00:24:39.883 --> 00:24:42.008
Is this the apartment you told me about?


00:24:42.092 --> 00:24:44.758
No, it's a 2-bedroom here.


00:24:44.883 --> 00:24:47.133
$250 a month more.


00:24:47.383 --> 00:24:50.675
The other one was a dump. Nowhere to put a crib.


00:24:50.758 --> 00:24:52.050
Totally insane.


00:24:52.258 --> 00:24:54.717
Dump, I don't think so.


00:24:55.425 --> 00:24:57.758
Basic, maybe.


00:24:58.300 --> 00:24:59.425
Dump, definitely not.


00:25:01.467 --> 00:25:03.050
Basic, sure.


00:25:06.008 --> 00:25:08.925
You realize having a child is all about suffering?


00:25:09.258 --> 00:25:11.550
Vincent's birth was sheer hell.


00:25:11.675 --> 00:25:12.967
Torture.


00:25:13.383 --> 00:25:14.550
Three hours of agony.


00:25:14.592 --> 00:25:16.592
If you don't want to help us, don't.


00:25:17.175 --> 00:25:18.050
Nobody's forcing you.


00:25:18.133 --> 00:25:20.217
How'll you get by if I don't?


00:25:21.717 --> 00:25:23.050
That's our problem.


00:25:23.300 --> 00:25:26.050
You can't talk to me like that and take my money.


00:25:26.133 --> 00:25:28.342
I don't give a shit about your money.


00:25:28.508 --> 00:25:29.925
I never asked for it.


00:25:31.842 --> 00:25:34.758
You just stand there, saying nothing, as usual!


00:25:35.050 --> 00:25:38.842
It's bullshit! When are you going to get off your ass?


00:25:43.467 --> 00:25:44.842
Butt out, you!


00:25:44.925 --> 00:25:47.258
You realize that this is impossible?


00:25:47.342 --> 00:25:48.758
-What? -She's a lunatic.


00:25:48.842 --> 00:25:51.050
She's not. she's my girlfriend.


00:25:51.633 --> 00:25:53.550
You refuse to see I've changed.


00:25:55.592 --> 00:25:57.550
What do you feel now?


00:25:57.633 --> 00:25:59.300
Fear or anger?


00:25:59.383 --> 00:26:00.800
Anger.


00:26:01.508 --> 00:26:04.300
You've missed your wife. Anna's in Angoulême today.


00:26:07.717 --> 00:26:09.383
And you knew it.


00:26:22.175 --> 00:26:24.842
You know I went through a traumatic
experience...


00:26:25.217 --> 00:26:26.342
Recently.


00:26:27.550 --> 00:26:30.925
You gave the impression of soldiering on like nothing happened.


00:26:32.717 --> 00:26:34.800
If I seem insensitive, I'm sorry.


00:26:34.883 --> 00:26:36.467
That's just me, right?


00:26:37.717 --> 00:26:39.425
I see you're staying in character.


00:26:39.758 --> 00:26:43.342
A big part of my character


00:26:54.592 --> 00:26:57.967
is being unpredictable.


00:27:01.717 --> 00:27:02.758
Hold on.


00:28:57.633 --> 00:29:00.758
Say, have you experienced any incidents recently?


00:29:00.842 --> 00:29:01.592
Incidents?


00:29:01.675 --> 00:29:03.300
You know what I mean.


00:29:03.383 --> 00:29:06.758
A man threw pizza at me from his car. He missed.


00:29:06.925 --> 00:29:10.050
People were staring at me at the market.


00:29:10.258 --> 00:29:11.800
But I always feel that.


00:29:12.383 --> 00:29:14.592
I wonder if it isn't starting again.


00:29:15.050 --> 00:29:16.508
A new cycle.


00:29:16.675 --> 00:29:18.050
You don't know?


00:29:18.467 --> 00:29:22.258
The Accused Will Rise about your father aired again last Saturday.


00:29:22.342 --> 00:29:25.050
- Refreshes people's memories.
- I'd no idea.


00:29:25.508 --> 00:29:26.592
And you?


00:29:27.050 --> 00:29:28.925
Anything happened?


00:29:29.008 --> 00:29:30.508
No, nothing special.


00:29:32.467 --> 00:29:34.342
It's because of his parole hearing.


00:29:34.550 --> 00:29:36.050
A media feeding frenzy.


00:29:36.300 --> 00:29:38.092
He's up before the judge next week.


00:29:38.717 --> 00:29:39.883
You don't miss a beat.


00:29:39.967 --> 00:29:41.925
Two coffees, please.


00:29:42.300 --> 00:29:43.508
Come with me.


00:29:43.592 --> 00:29:46.550
They'll never let him out. Thank god!


00:29:47.092 --> 00:29:49.258
The parole hearing is a charade.


00:29:49.342 --> 00:29:51.008
Like you telling me to come,


00:29:51.092 --> 00:29:53.425
when you know I'd rather gouge my eyes out.


00:29:53.508 --> 00:29:55.258
How long will you hang on to hatred?


00:29:55.342 --> 00:29:58.675
I'll never see him again, in this world or any other.


00:29:58.758 --> 00:30:00.508
- Anyway, there is no other.
- Your coffee.


00:30:00.592 --> 00:30:02.508
- There isn't much time left.
- Thanks.


00:30:02.592 --> 00:30:03.717
He's ill.


00:30:04.883 --> 00:30:06.133
Look...


00:30:07.342 --> 00:30:08.967
Look, just for one moment.


00:30:10.758 --> 00:30:12.842
You're afraid to look at your own father?


00:30:21.133 --> 00:30:22.675
Put it away now.


00:30:24.258 --> 00:30:25.675
You're not like the mob.


00:30:26.008 --> 00:30:28.092
People who only know the monster.


00:30:28.550 --> 00:30:31.050
You know the man. He's just a man.


00:30:31.133 --> 00:30:33.050
Who happens to be a monster.


00:30:33.133 --> 00:30:35.092
You see a contradiction there?


00:30:36.758 --> 00:30:38.883
Drink up. I'm done here.


00:30:39.925 --> 00:30:41.383
Be careful, won't you?


00:30:41.717 --> 00:30:44.383
Some people won't just toss crap


00:30:44.467 --> 00:30:45.883
from their cars.


00:31:51.342 --> 00:31:52.675
Marty!


00:31:56.925 --> 00:31:58.342
Give me that bird.


00:31:59.050 --> 00:32:00.383
Marty!


00:32:01.842 --> 00:32:04.258
We don't treat wild birds. It's a sparrow?


00:32:04.800 --> 00:32:05.758
Yes.


00:32:06.675 --> 00:32:09.592
I wouldn't even know how to intubate your sparrow.


00:32:09.675 --> 00:32:11.258
If it is a sparrow.


00:32:13.508 --> 00:32:15.092
Thanks very much.


00:32:15.342 --> 00:32:16.217
Goodbye.


00:32:16.300 --> 00:32:17.758
You're welcome. Goodbye.


00:32:34.300 --> 00:32:36.133
...victims of all ages.


00:32:36.717 --> 00:32:40.675
Seen today, this quiet street in the suburbs of Nantes


00:32:40.842 --> 00:32:44.383
bears no trace of the atrocities that took place here


00:32:44.467 --> 00:32:45.883
39 years ago.


00:32:46.592 --> 00:32:48.467
Few of today's inhabitants


00:32:48.550 --> 00:32:50.092
know the name, Georges Leblanc.


00:32:50.633 --> 00:32:52.133
Or if they do,


00:32:52.717 --> 00:32:55.508
it's a name associated with a horror story


00:32:55.592 --> 00:32:57.342
that they can hardly remember.


00:32:57.800 --> 00:33:00.508
An urban folktale from another time.


00:33:00.883 --> 00:33:03.217
And yet, in 1976,


00:33:03.300 --> 00:33:06.425
the eyes of France were trained on this street.


00:33:07.092 --> 00:33:08.883
A nation held its breath.


00:33:09.008 --> 00:33:10.508
In shock.


00:33:11.092 --> 00:33:12.508
Time has dulled the terror


00:33:12.592 --> 00:33:14.675
of that distant day in May.


00:33:15.092 --> 00:33:18.050
But for some the horror will never fade away.


00:33:18.592 --> 00:33:20.717
Nor will the unanswered questions.


00:33:21.467 --> 00:33:23.800
What drove Georges Leblanc,


00:33:23.925 --> 00:33:25.383
a practising Catholic,


00:33:25.467 --> 00:33:27.217
loving husband and father,


00:33:27.300 --> 00:33:30.383
to commit such monstrous and senseless acts?


00:33:31.175 --> 00:33:35.550
And what role exactly was played by his daughter, Michèle?


00:33:36.092 --> 00:33:38.383
A ten-year-old child at the time.


00:33:42.175 --> 00:33:44.842
After years of trials and psychiatric evaluations,


00:33:44.883 --> 00:33:47.925
over 30 years after Georges Leblanc's incarceration,


00:33:47.967 --> 00:33:49.883
sentenced to life,


00:33:50.050 --> 00:33:52.925
the questions remain,


00:33:53.175 --> 00:33:54.592
as banal yet chilling as ever.


00:33:55.217 --> 00:33:56.300
First and foremost...


00:33:56.633 --> 00:33:57.675
Why?


00:33:57.758 --> 00:33:59.258
Murderer!


00:34:15.383 --> 00:34:17.050
I hope that's recyclable.


00:34:17.758 --> 00:34:19.217
It's a dead bird.


00:35:50.258 --> 00:35:51.508
Richard!


00:35:56.342 --> 00:35:57.800
What were you thinking?


00:35:58.008 --> 00:35:59.717
I was worried about you.


00:35:59.800 --> 00:36:00.925
Jesus!


00:36:01.175 --> 00:36:02.925
Don't rub your eyes.


00:36:06.675 --> 00:36:08.800
You say you were raped and didn't report it,


00:36:08.883 --> 00:36:10.258
obviously I'm going to...


00:36:10.717 --> 00:36:13.508
Holy shit, you really did a number on me!


00:36:13.592 --> 00:36:15.175
I'm sorry.


00:36:15.925 --> 00:36:18.133
That helps? You know what you're doing?


00:36:18.217 --> 00:36:20.342
It's on the pepper spray label.


00:36:20.508 --> 00:36:21.800
Could be, I'll go blind.


00:36:21.883 --> 00:36:23.675
Of course, you won't go blind!


00:36:24.633 --> 00:36:25.842
There we go.


00:36:28.050 --> 00:36:30.175
- Glass of wine?
- Yes, please.


00:36:31.508 --> 00:36:34.092
I didn't recognize the car. Whose is it?


00:36:34.258 --> 00:36:35.550
A friend's.


00:36:35.967 --> 00:36:37.092
A girl friend's?


00:36:38.217 --> 00:36:40.342
- Her name's Hélène.
- Hélène.


00:36:42.842 --> 00:36:45.092
I borrowed hers. Mine's in the shop.


00:36:45.258 --> 00:36:47.008
Somebody smashed the bumper.


00:36:48.342 --> 00:36:49.675
It was barely visible.


00:36:54.592 --> 00:36:56.217
She's a friend, Michèle.


00:36:56.300 --> 00:36:58.008
Why am I even justifying this?


00:36:58.092 --> 00:36:59.717
You have nothing to justify.


00:37:01.342 --> 00:37:03.592
- She's a student?
- Grad student.


00:37:04.133 --> 00:37:05.550
Surprise me.


00:37:05.717 --> 00:37:09.217
She's not my student. She organizes a De Beauvoir seminar.


00:37:09.300 --> 00:37:10.758
She invited me to speak.


00:37:10.967 --> 00:37:12.175
And she's read your book.


00:37:12.258 --> 00:37:13.342
She's read it.


00:37:13.425 --> 00:37:15.800
And told me how deeply it touched her,


00:37:15.883 --> 00:37:17.758
I melted inside.


00:37:17.842 --> 00:37:20.342
That's all. You can imagine the rest.


00:37:20.425 --> 00:37:22.550
I can imagine just fine, actually.


00:37:23.258 --> 00:37:24.967
Your jealousy is insane.


00:37:25.050 --> 00:37:27.008
No, I'm just concerned.


00:37:28.967 --> 00:37:32.092
I'm concerned because this is what I feared.


00:37:33.050 --> 00:37:35.300
The bimbos with big tits never worried me,


00:37:35.383 --> 00:37:39.092
but a woman who's read:
"The Second Sex" will chew you up...


00:37:39.758 --> 00:37:40.967
And spit you out.


00:37:41.133 --> 00:37:43.425
The real danger, Michèle, is you.


00:37:47.592 --> 00:37:49.467
Did you know about her?


00:37:49.550 --> 00:37:51.175
Yeah, I met her once.


00:37:51.258 --> 00:37:52.758
When was that?


00:37:52.842 --> 00:37:56.258
Last week. We all had dinner at Dad's.


00:37:57.008 --> 00:37:58.425
Why didn't you mention it?


00:37:58.508 --> 00:37:59.800
I dunno...


00:37:59.883 --> 00:38:01.342
Josie, put that down. I'll do it.


00:38:01.550 --> 00:38:02.925
When?


00:38:03.050 --> 00:38:05.425
Can I have some focus here, please?


00:38:05.592 --> 00:38:06.342
What?


00:38:06.925 --> 00:38:08.217
What's Hélène like?


00:38:08.342 --> 00:38:11.967
She's cool. A yoga teacher.
Bikram yoga, I think.


00:38:12.050 --> 00:38:13.467
Move your feet, will you?


00:38:13.883 --> 00:38:14.717
Where?


00:38:14.800 --> 00:38:17.425
- Why?
- I told Eric he could have it.


00:38:17.467 --> 00:38:19.133
Eric? Who's this Eric?


00:38:19.217 --> 00:38:20.467
Marais Yoga Center.


00:38:20.550 --> 00:38:23.217
-Can't it wait? -Move your feet!


00:38:25.300 --> 00:38:27.300
How about you help me unpack?


00:38:27.383 --> 00:38:28.758
I'll be right there.


00:38:28.842 --> 00:38:30.883
The fight'll be over in 10 minutes.


00:38:30.967 --> 00:38:32.800
And soccer next up.


00:38:38.875 --> 00:38:40.833
Josie! Where are you going?


00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:43.917
Vincent, I'll call you back.


00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:45.333
Yeah. bye.


00:38:54.875 --> 00:38:56.000
Seen it?


00:38:56.417 --> 00:38:58.292
It was sent to the whole office?


00:38:58.375 --> 00:38:59.458
Take a look.


00:39:13.583 --> 00:39:15.625
This isn't the first thing he's sent me.


00:39:16.292 --> 00:39:17.958
First thing who's sent you?


00:39:20.208 --> 00:39:21.750
The guy who attacked you?


00:39:21.833 --> 00:39:23.208
Of course.


00:39:23.417 --> 00:39:26.083
You think that's possible? Your attacker?


00:39:26.458 --> 00:39:29.500
I mean, the email seems to come from here.


00:39:29.583 --> 00:39:30.833
Looks like it.


00:39:31.333 --> 00:39:32.625
Call the police now.


00:39:32.708 --> 00:39:35.417
The police, never again. It's pointless.


00:39:35.500 --> 00:39:37.708
This is different. You're the victim.


00:39:37.792 --> 00:39:39.667
I was the victim then!


00:39:40.625 --> 00:39:41.708
Sorry, I...


00:39:41.750 --> 00:39:43.500
I don't want the police involved.


00:39:43.583 --> 00:39:46.125
I won't let this cretin stir up all that shit.


00:39:46.292 --> 00:39:50.167
I fought too hard to rebuild my life, so police, journalists...


00:39:50.792 --> 00:39:52.083
No way.


00:39:52.583 --> 00:39:53.542
God help us.


00:39:53.667 --> 00:39:55.125
There's a nutjob out there.


00:39:55.208 --> 00:39:57.792
Nutjobs, I can handle. My specialty.


00:39:58.917 --> 00:40:00.625
When our server was hacked in June,


00:40:04.708 --> 00:40:08.375
somebody ripped the Cthulhu template off our mainframe.


00:40:08.833 --> 00:40:10.958
Images like these have floated around since then.


00:40:12.208 --> 00:40:13.750
My secret admirer...


00:40:13.833 --> 00:40:15.833
Must be highly tech savvy.


00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:19.958
- A former employee maybe?
- Yeah.


00:40:24.833 --> 00:40:27.083
Last question. You think she's pretty?


00:40:29.542 --> 00:40:31.458
Bend forward, from low in your back.


00:40:31.542 --> 00:40:34.458
Stretch your spine all the way to the floor.


00:40:35.125 --> 00:40:36.250
Deep breath.


00:40:36.333 --> 00:40:39.958
Push the floor with your left hand until seated again.


00:40:40.042 --> 00:40:41.500
Thank you all very much.


00:40:41.583 --> 00:40:44.250
Have a good day. Excellent work.


00:40:46.167 --> 00:40:47.125
Namaste.


00:40:48.667 --> 00:40:49.583
Hélène?


00:40:50.458 --> 00:40:53.875
I'm Michèle. Richard's ex.


00:40:55.458 --> 00:40:57.708
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.


00:40:57.792 --> 00:41:00.250
Hope you don't mind me barging in.


00:41:00.333 --> 00:41:03.333
I wanted to apologize face to face.


00:41:03.583 --> 00:41:04.500
For what?


00:41:04.583 --> 00:41:06.792
Your car window. I'm sorry.


00:41:06.917 --> 00:41:11.333
Please. it's nothing. Anyway, Richard explained it all.


00:41:12.083 --> 00:41:14.333
Really? What was his explanation?


00:41:14.417 --> 00:41:16.542
It was an accident.


00:41:17.625 --> 00:41:20.292
Yes, that's right. An accident.


00:41:21.083 --> 00:41:23.250
And a good chance to meet you.


00:41:23.333 --> 00:41:24.500
Yes, great!


00:41:24.542 --> 00:41:26.958
It's wonderful finally meeting you.


00:41:27.125 --> 00:41:30.208
- I was thinking...
- Richard won't have to introduce us.


00:41:30.292 --> 00:41:32.375
We've dodged an awkward situation.


00:41:33.167 --> 00:41:35.417
Why would it be awkward?


00:41:36.250 --> 00:41:37.708
Well...


00:41:37.792 --> 00:41:39.750
Of course, you're right, it's...


00:41:40.083 --> 00:41:42.000
I guess we could have...


00:41:42.083 --> 00:41:44.875
- I mean...
- But it's behind us now.


00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:45.917
Exactly!


00:41:48.708 --> 00:41:51.833
We should get together some time, all of us.


00:41:52.500 --> 00:41:54.333
Yes. I'm having a Christmas party.


00:41:54.417 --> 00:41:56.708
You really must come.


00:41:57.042 --> 00:41:58.417
Come along.


00:41:58.958 --> 00:42:00.125
If I must.


00:42:00.292 --> 00:42:03.542
I'll give Richard the details.
I should get going.


00:42:04.167 --> 00:42:05.500
Lovely to meet you.


00:42:05.583 --> 00:42:07.625
Yes, lovely to have met you.


00:42:07.708 --> 00:42:09.083
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.


00:42:21.167 --> 00:42:21.875
Hello?


00:42:26.042 --> 00:42:27.667
Port Royal, right now?


00:42:29.417 --> 00:42:30.542
Really?


00:42:34.083 --> 00:42:36.417
She was losing blood. They did an ultrasound.


00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:38.958
- She has a...
- A placental abruption.


00:42:39.042 --> 00:42:41.458
They say it's okay but they're inducing labor.


00:42:41.542 --> 00:42:43.292
- Oh.
- Omar, a buddy of mine.


00:42:43.375 --> 00:42:44.583
- Hello.
- Dad!


00:42:44.667 --> 00:42:47.333
- What's the news?
- Nothing yet.


00:42:48.667 --> 00:42:50.750
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:42:50.833 --> 00:42:52.167
I'm right here.


00:42:52.250 --> 00:42:55.167
- I'm scared.
- It's gonna be okay.


00:42:56.667 --> 00:42:58.375
It hurts!


00:42:59.292 --> 00:43:00.958
I'll go get a coffee.


00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:02.458
Deep breaths.


00:43:02.542 --> 00:43:04.917
Fuck, it hurts!


00:43:05.542 --> 00:43:08.167
So suddenly you're throwing a Christmas party?


00:43:08.417 --> 00:43:12.000
I thought it'd be good to get to know each other better.


00:43:12.083 --> 00:43:13.417
She's lovely, by the way.


00:43:13.500 --> 00:43:14.708
Another of your traps?


00:43:14.792 --> 00:43:18.958
I have better things to do than
plot diabolical Christmas dinners.


00:43:20.083 --> 00:43:22.583
Is there anything she won't eat?
Any allergies?


00:43:22.708 --> 00:43:25.083
The cat's shedding like crazy.


00:43:26.792 --> 00:43:28.667
I made no fuss about your violinist.


00:43:28.750 --> 00:43:30.083
That was different!


00:43:30.167 --> 00:43:33.417
He was married with 3 kids. He checked every box.


00:43:33.833 --> 00:43:36.417
She's a young, single woman of child-bearing age.


00:43:36.500 --> 00:43:37.708
You've broken all the rules.


00:43:37.792 --> 00:43:41.083
First I heard we had an agreement.
It's not my fault if...


00:43:42.167 --> 00:43:45.333
It is your fault. We should still be together.


00:43:46.208 --> 00:43:48.417
- It's your fault.
- You left me.


00:43:48.500 --> 00:43:49.833
You hit me.


00:43:52.583 --> 00:43:55.750
If there's one thing in my life I regret, it's that.


00:43:57.333 --> 00:43:58.250
All done!


00:43:58.667 --> 00:44:00.125
- All done?
- Yes.


00:44:18.083 --> 00:44:20.750
We're going to need a DNA test.


00:44:32.083 --> 00:44:34.708
- Are they bringing him in?
- Right now.


00:44:35.167 --> 00:44:36.958
I'll be a good mother to him.


00:44:37.208 --> 00:44:39.000
Silly! You'll be awesome!


00:44:57.167 --> 00:44:58.333
Should we go?


00:44:59.833 --> 00:45:00.917
No.


00:45:01.083 --> 00:45:02.458
It's fine.


00:45:02.833 --> 00:45:04.333
Lots of people here.


00:45:13.542 --> 00:45:15.042
Hey, everybody!


00:45:19.458 --> 00:45:21.250
Who's a proud Daddy!


00:45:26.625 --> 00:45:29.708
A little marvel! Isn't he handsome!


00:45:29.792 --> 00:45:31.750
Look at that!


00:45:34.750 --> 00:45:36.750
This is where I had my son.


00:45:37.375 --> 00:45:38.792
In this maternity unit.


00:45:38.958 --> 00:45:40.208
That's funny.


00:45:40.708 --> 00:45:42.458
Not really. The amazing thing is,


00:45:42.542 --> 00:45:43.583
my friend Anna...


00:45:43.667 --> 00:45:46.667
- You saw her up there, you met her.
- Yes.


00:45:47.375 --> 00:45:49.958
She gave birth here that same night.


00:45:51.333 --> 00:45:53.333
This is where we met.


00:45:54.083 --> 00:45:57.042
Her child was still born. She asked to breastfeed mine.


00:45:57.750 --> 00:45:58.667
Oh my!


00:45:59.708 --> 00:46:02.000
I said to her, fine.


00:46:02.625 --> 00:46:05.125
Since then, I've often wondered.


00:46:06.042 --> 00:46:07.958
They've always been very close.


00:46:08.583 --> 00:46:10.042
Anna and my son.


00:46:10.958 --> 00:46:13.542
I wonder if there wasn't some kind of


00:46:14.792 --> 00:46:17.167
imprinting, like with ducks.


00:46:19.792 --> 00:46:21.667
With me. on the other hand...


00:46:21.958 --> 00:46:24.292
- You know...
- Sorry, they're paging me.


00:46:26.000 --> 00:46:27.583
Sometimes I look at Vincent,


00:46:28.042 --> 00:46:31.375
the big lout with nothing special about him


00:46:31.875 --> 00:46:33.500
that came out of my belly,


00:46:34.583 --> 00:46:36.583
and I have to admit I don't know him.


00:46:56.458 --> 00:46:58.417
- Evening, Michèle.
- Evening, Rebecca.


00:46:58.500 --> 00:47:01.167
Patrick will walk you inside. There's a prowler.


00:47:01.250 --> 00:47:04.000
- There is?
- Patrick fought with him.


00:47:04.083 --> 00:47:05.875
- A prowler?
- Yes.


00:47:05.917 --> 00:47:08.625
They're sending 3 cars after the creep.


00:47:09.000 --> 00:47:10.542
You fought with him?


00:47:10.625 --> 00:47:12.250
I caught him crouched in the bushes,


00:47:12.333 --> 00:47:14.083
watching your house.


00:47:14.167 --> 00:47:16.125
When I approached, he took off.


00:47:17.167 --> 00:47:18.583
You saw his face?


00:47:18.750 --> 00:47:21.542
No, he was wearing a mask, like a ski mask.


00:47:21.625 --> 00:47:23.625
Like a stalker on a TV show.


00:47:24.125 --> 00:47:25.125
He got away.


00:47:25.208 --> 00:47:27.208
Pat, go in with her.


00:47:27.292 --> 00:47:29.000
No, don't bother.


00:47:32.000 --> 00:47:34.667
- Do it anyway.
- Okay, be right back.


00:47:40.792 --> 00:47:42.917
It's really not necessary, honestly.


00:47:43.500 --> 00:47:45.583
I have pepper spray in the house.


00:47:46.000 --> 00:47:47.042
Good to know.


00:48:05.083 --> 00:48:07.417
Light switch on your left there.


00:48:19.208 --> 00:48:20.750
Everything seems to be okay.


00:48:21.000 --> 00:48:23.667
Thanks, anyway. I appreciate it.


00:48:23.875 --> 00:48:25.667
No problem, I didn't do much.


00:48:26.667 --> 00:48:27.667
I nearly caught him,


00:48:27.750 --> 00:48:29.333
but he took off so fast.


00:48:31.042 --> 00:48:33.792
In high school, I ran the 1,000 meters in 2.42.


00:48:36.375 --> 00:48:39.292
Perhaps his speed shows how scared he was of you.


00:48:41.417 --> 00:48:43.875
Thank you for salvaging my pride.


00:48:44.208 --> 00:48:45.375
You're welcome.


00:48:52.625 --> 00:48:53.708
Well...


00:49:02.833 --> 00:49:05.000
See anything or hear anything, just shout.


00:49:05.083 --> 00:49:06.167
Okay.


00:49:09.833 --> 00:49:11.333
I'm a grandmother.


00:49:13.083 --> 00:49:15.208
-Congratulations. -Thank you.


00:49:26.750 --> 00:49:28.708
God knows why I said that.


00:49:55.292 --> 00:49:56.625
Morning, Michèle.


00:49:59.417 --> 00:50:00.917
I like your sweater.


00:50:02.250 --> 00:50:03.250
Do you ski?


00:50:05.000 --> 00:50:05.875
Sure.


00:50:06.917 --> 00:50:08.125
I'll take you anytime.


00:50:31.583 --> 00:50:32.667
Kevin?


00:50:33.417 --> 00:50:35.167
You shoot, right?


00:50:36.083 --> 00:50:38.042
I mean. real shooting.


00:50:38.375 --> 00:50:39.792
That's right, I do.


00:50:40.625 --> 00:50:42.292
You own guns?


00:50:43.375 --> 00:50:44.792
A couple.


00:50:48.083 --> 00:50:49.625
Could you teach me?


00:50:50.292 --> 00:50:51.625
I could show you, sure.


00:50:57.917 --> 00:50:59.750
In real life, that'd do the job.


00:51:00.083 --> 00:51:02.500
In real life, he'd run faster.


00:51:03.000 --> 00:51:04.042
True.


00:51:04.792 --> 00:51:06.250
Try the .44 now.


00:51:14.000 --> 00:51:16.125
Kevin, I also wanted to talk to you


00:51:16.208 --> 00:51:19.333
because I've got an unofficial assignment for you.


00:51:19.583 --> 00:51:21.250
A black op?


00:51:22.583 --> 00:51:25.833
I want to know who created that animation.


00:51:27.292 --> 00:51:28.625
You know the one I mean?


00:51:30.458 --> 00:51:34.000
Hack into the home computers of the whole office.


00:51:34.625 --> 00:51:36.500
All the guys, at least.


00:51:37.917 --> 00:51:41.667
I want to help, but that's a major violation.


00:51:41.750 --> 00:51:44.542
I'm offering $10,000 cash in hand.


00:51:45.792 --> 00:51:48.292
Between you and me. Our secret.


00:51:51.208 --> 00:51:54.833
When you snoop on people, you turn up some weird shit.


00:51:54.917 --> 00:51:57.625
I know. I won't judge.


00:52:00.083 --> 00:52:01.458
Where does this one go?


00:52:01.792 --> 00:52:03.417
Put it right there.


00:54:01.083 --> 00:54:02.958
I untangled that one. Try it.


00:54:03.167 --> 00:54:06.208
- This one?
- On the right. I'll do the other next.


00:54:06.708 --> 00:54:08.708
-Hi, Rebecca! -Hi. Michèle.


00:54:08.792 --> 00:54:10.833
Beautiful!


00:54:11.250 --> 00:54:12.917
- Evening.
- Evening.


00:54:13.625 --> 00:54:17.125
The Nativity gets me every time. Where it all began.


00:54:18.083 --> 00:54:20.375
Very true.


00:54:22.375 --> 00:54:25.458
I know it's rude to invite you last minute,


00:54:25.542 --> 00:54:28.750
but I'm having a Christmas get-together tomorrow.


00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:30.583
Patrick, did you hear that?


00:54:30.667 --> 00:54:31.625
Yeah.


00:54:33.375 --> 00:54:34.500
With pleasure.


00:54:34.583 --> 00:54:35.875
Yes, with pleasure, absolutely.


00:54:35.958 --> 00:54:38.958
Well then...


00:54:39.500 --> 00:54:40.542
See you tomorrow.


00:54:40.625 --> 00:54:41.958
- See you then.
- See you then.


00:54:42.000 --> 00:54:43.000
Thank you.


00:54:50.292 --> 00:54:52.208
In theory, we could put a toothpick


00:54:52.292 --> 00:54:54.042
inside one for Richard's ladylove.


00:54:54.917 --> 00:54:56.625
Or just poison her.


00:54:56.708 --> 00:54:59.208
She has me pegged as a Medea, She'd see it coming.


00:54:59.292 --> 00:55:00.667
Consumed by jealousy.


00:55:01.083 --> 00:55:02.958
She was a classics major, too?


00:55:07.750 --> 00:55:09.917
-Josie. -Robert.


00:55:10.375 --> 00:55:11.292
Merry Christmas!


00:55:11.375 --> 00:55:12.708
- Okay, Dad?
- Great.


00:55:12.792 --> 00:55:13.833
Hi, kiddo.


00:55:13.917 --> 00:55:16.333
Jeez, he stinks. Here!


00:55:17.958 --> 00:55:19.292
How you doing?


00:55:20.375 --> 00:55:23.750
You trying to deafen us all with your shit? Careful.


00:55:23.833 --> 00:55:25.167
Hello, all!


00:55:25.875 --> 00:55:27.708
Merry Christmas!


00:55:32.083 --> 00:55:35.125
If I ever show up like that, kill me.


00:55:35.250 --> 00:55:36.583
Evening!


00:55:38.958 --> 00:55:40.292
- Evening!
- Evening!


00:55:40.458 --> 00:55:42.958
Sorry we're late. I was digging out a great...


00:55:43.042 --> 00:55:44.000
Excuse me.


00:55:44.583 --> 00:55:45.708
Cabernet.


00:55:48.042 --> 00:55:49.792
- Evening!
- Evening!


00:55:50.042 --> 00:55:51.500
Scrabble party!


00:55:53.333 --> 00:55:54.667
Thank you.


00:55:54.750 --> 00:55:55.750
- Evening!
- Evening!


00:55:55.875 --> 00:55:57.250
Any more alerts?


00:55:57.333 --> 00:55:59.500
No, the bogeyman's deserted us.


00:55:59.583 --> 00:56:02.542
Anyway, we're safe tonight.


00:56:02.625 --> 00:56:05.208
I got my red belt in March.


00:56:05.917 --> 00:56:09.458
I did Taekwondo for years before switching to Shotokan.


00:56:09.542 --> 00:56:11.042
I've never done karate.


00:56:11.250 --> 00:56:13.000
She was making fun of me.


00:56:13.750 --> 00:56:14.667
Ok.


00:56:18.958 --> 00:56:21.125
You can't avoid me all night.


00:56:21.250 --> 00:56:22.208
Want a bet?


00:56:29.875 --> 00:56:31.083
I'm glad you made it.


00:56:31.167 --> 00:56:32.875
We don't get out much.


00:56:32.958 --> 00:56:36.000
Unfortunately for Rebecca, who's a very social person.


00:56:36.708 --> 00:56:38.042
Unlike me.


00:56:38.625 --> 00:56:41.250
I'm glad she dragged you over here tonight.


00:56:43.250 --> 00:56:44.875
It was no hardship.


00:56:46.208 --> 00:56:47.375
Good evening!


00:56:47.917 --> 00:56:49.667
So sorry I'm late.


00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:51.458
I couldn't get off work.


00:56:51.542 --> 00:56:53.708
We just sat down. Hi, Hélène.


00:56:53.792 --> 00:56:55.000
- Evening!
- Evening!


00:56:55.083 --> 00:56:56.667
Evening, everybody.


00:56:56.750 --> 00:56:57.958
Irène, this is Hélène.


00:56:58.042 --> 00:56:59.458
- Evening!
- Evening!


00:56:59.542 --> 00:57:01.375
- Evening. I'm Ralf.
- Evening.


00:57:02.958 --> 00:57:04.708
Well, enjoy your meal!


00:57:04.958 --> 00:57:05.833
Thanks.


00:57:06.750 --> 00:57:08.208
I'm sorry...


00:57:08.417 --> 00:57:11.792
I'd like to say grace, if nobody objects.


00:57:13.625 --> 00:57:15.250
Of course not. Please do.


00:57:15.375 --> 00:57:16.792
Thank you.


00:57:19.708 --> 00:57:22.333
Bless us, Lord, and bless this meal.


00:57:22.917 --> 00:57:24.625
And provide bread to the needy.


00:57:25.375 --> 00:57:26.375
Amen.


00:57:26.458 --> 00:57:28.417
- Amen.
- Amen.


00:57:28.708 --> 00:57:29.875
Wine, Michèle?


00:57:29.958 --> 00:57:31.417
With pleasure.


00:57:31.958 --> 00:57:33.583
So, Patrick, what do you do?


00:57:33.792 --> 00:57:35.083
I work in banking.


00:57:36.000 --> 00:57:38.792
I'm a broker. And I plead guilty.


00:57:39.292 --> 00:57:40.333
How come?


00:57:40.833 --> 00:57:44.792
Just joking. It's not a popular profession right now.


00:57:44.958 --> 00:57:46.333
It never was.


00:57:47.667 --> 00:57:49.500
- I guess not.
- Well.


00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:51.167
To Christmas!


00:57:51.500 --> 00:57:52.542
And to us!


00:57:52.625 --> 00:57:56.875
Especially the newcomers to our table...


00:57:57.083 --> 00:57:58.208
Irène,


00:57:59.292 --> 00:58:00.458
Patrick,


00:58:00.708 --> 00:58:02.042
Rebecca.


00:58:05.750 --> 00:58:06.667
Ralf.


00:58:07.500 --> 00:58:08.375
Ralf.


00:58:08.958 --> 00:58:10.000
Merry Christmas!


00:58:10.333 --> 00:58:12.083
Merry Christmas!


00:58:14.000 --> 00:58:17.000
Michèle's worked like a trooper.


00:58:17.083 --> 00:58:18.042
Absolutely.


00:58:18.667 --> 00:58:20.208
I love cooking.


00:58:20.667 --> 00:58:21.625
When are you going?


00:58:21.708 --> 00:58:24.875
I'll try to book the...


00:58:26.667 --> 00:58:29.458
But the period we want books up fast.


00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:33.167
People don't realize the art muscle needs training.


00:58:33.250 --> 00:58:35.917
Or else culture collapses, goes flabby.


00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:38.792
That's what we've got now. Flabby culture.


00:58:39.042 --> 00:58:40.625
Is that aimed at me?


00:58:40.708 --> 00:58:42.250
Originality or singularity


00:58:42.333 --> 00:58:45.458
used to be valued and sought after.


00:58:45.667 --> 00:58:48.792
Or even an end in itself.
Now it's a liability.


00:58:48.875 --> 00:58:50.458
Richard's a theorist.


00:58:50.583 --> 00:58:52.708
I'm not talking about novelty.


00:58:52.792 --> 00:58:55.167
Coming out of our ass, novelty!


00:58:55.250 --> 00:58:56.958
Delightful image at dinner.


00:58:57.042 --> 00:59:00.042
Anyway, what's inspiration? 80% hard work.


00:59:00.125 --> 00:59:03.000
Some people know nothing of hard work.


00:59:03.083 --> 00:59:04.208
It's not in their culture.


00:59:04.292 --> 00:59:06.375
We know who you mean.


00:59:07.292 --> 00:59:08.750
I didn't say a word.


00:59:08.875 --> 00:59:11.167
Everybody's different. I love everyone.


00:59:15.250 --> 00:59:16.708
We're all children of God!


00:59:16.792 --> 00:59:20.458
Yeah, Africans eat goat's innards.
They're different.


00:59:20.542 --> 00:59:21.458
Exactly.


00:59:21.500 --> 00:59:23.875
I went on safari in Kenya. It was great.


00:59:23.958 --> 00:59:25.458
Right, there you go.


00:59:25.500 --> 00:59:27.042
I think now is a good time.


00:59:28.333 --> 00:59:30.042
I have an announcement to make.


00:59:32.167 --> 00:59:35.333
Ralf and I are engaged to be married.


00:59:45.917 --> 00:59:46.875
Sorry.


00:59:49.750 --> 00:59:51.958
How do you manage to be so grotesque?


00:59:53.583 --> 00:59:54.917
Don't you realize?


00:59:57.125 --> 00:59:59.208
I hope everyone likes blueberries.


01:00:00.667 --> 01:00:03.542
Josie added a ton to the official recipe.


01:00:03.625 --> 01:00:07.750
I was feeling creative, so I added blueberries.


01:00:10.417 --> 01:00:11.875
Looks good to me.


01:00:15.875 --> 01:00:19.208
It's almost midnight. Do you mind if I put on the Mass?


01:00:19.292 --> 01:00:20.542
On the contrary.


01:00:27.125 --> 01:00:28.250
You're leaving?


01:00:29.250 --> 01:00:30.792
It was wonderful. Really.


01:00:31.292 --> 01:00:33.292
Next time, our turn. You'll come to us.


01:00:33.375 --> 01:00:35.250
Let's not rush things.


01:00:35.333 --> 01:00:36.292
Leave it to us.


01:00:36.375 --> 01:00:40.292
We'll have lunch first, Michèle and I.


01:00:40.542 --> 01:00:41.542
Just the two of us.


01:00:41.958 --> 01:00:43.792
One step at a time.


01:00:43.917 --> 01:00:45.583
I agree, excellent idea.


01:00:45.917 --> 01:00:46.708
Goodnight.


01:00:46.792 --> 01:00:47.750
Great.


01:00:48.542 --> 01:00:49.875
- See you!
- See you!


01:00:52.083 --> 01:00:53.583
See you, 'night!


01:00:56.417 --> 01:00:58.875
Flirting with the banker, was that a test?


01:00:59.000 --> 01:01:02.375
You're making a scene in my home? It's come to that?


01:01:04.750 --> 01:01:07.250
- We'll talk later.
- Make yourself useful.


01:01:20.417 --> 01:01:21.500
Disaster!


01:01:21.542 --> 01:01:24.083
-That's two double words. -One double word.


01:01:24.167 --> 01:01:25.750
I can top that.


01:01:25.833 --> 01:01:27.375
Journey!


01:01:27.875 --> 01:01:29.750
- 64.
- Hold on, I've got it.


01:01:29.833 --> 01:01:31.000
No, that's 70.


01:01:31.042 --> 01:01:32.708
70, you see.


01:01:32.792 --> 01:01:34.000
My bad.


01:01:34.250 --> 01:01:36.000
- Ladies...
- No, thanks.


01:01:36.042 --> 01:01:37.708
- Sure?
- Really.


01:01:42.625 --> 01:01:44.708
Curse him! Damn him!


01:01:44.792 --> 01:01:48.250
Close the book, ring the bell, blow out the candle.


01:01:49.417 --> 01:01:50.458
What's that?


01:01:51.125 --> 01:01:52.208
Call yourself a Catholic?


01:01:52.292 --> 01:01:54.542
You don't know the excommunication rite?


01:01:55.583 --> 01:01:56.583
And you do?


01:01:58.083 --> 01:01:59.792
I've heard about it.


01:02:01.000 --> 01:02:03.208
My father made the sign of the cross on me,


01:02:03.750 --> 01:02:04.917
before I left for school.


01:02:05.167 --> 01:02:07.208
He did it to all the local kids


01:02:07.667 --> 01:02:10.042
until some parents asked him to stop.


01:02:10.125 --> 01:02:11.458
Sounds reasonable.


01:02:12.167 --> 01:02:14.542
Apparently, my father was offended.


01:02:15.250 --> 01:02:16.958
That night. he made the rounds.


01:02:18.167 --> 01:02:19.792
Knocked on every door,


01:02:20.208 --> 01:02:22.333
went into every house on the street


01:02:22.542 --> 01:02:24.000
with a shotgun, a butcher's mallet


01:02:24.083 --> 01:02:25.958
and a pair of kitchen knives.


01:02:26.875 --> 01:02:28.917
Yes, I heard about that.


01:02:29.208 --> 01:02:34.125
You heard about the 27 human victims, not about the animals.


01:02:34.500 --> 01:02:36.292
They never get a mention.


01:02:37.042 --> 01:02:38.083
6 dogs,


01:02:39.125 --> 01:02:40.708
a couple of cats, too.


01:02:41.792 --> 01:02:44.250
For whatever reason, he spared a hamster.


01:02:44.917 --> 01:02:46.417
You couldn't make it up.


01:02:52.292 --> 01:02:55.333
I was doing my homework when he arrived home


01:02:55.500 --> 01:02:57.042
with blood all over him.


01:02:57.958 --> 01:02:59.500
My mother was at work.


01:02:59.625 --> 01:03:01.875
She was a nurse back then.


01:03:02.167 --> 01:03:05.208
Can you imagine my mother. a nurse?


01:03:05.542 --> 01:03:07.083
Funny, isn't it?


01:03:07.292 --> 01:03:08.875
We don't have to go over it.


01:03:09.083 --> 01:03:12.167
I don't mind. It does me good to talk.


01:03:14.042 --> 01:03:16.292
He decided to burn everything in the house.


01:03:17.375 --> 01:03:18.792
I helped feed the fire.


01:03:18.875 --> 01:03:21.500
We gutted the place. Curtains, carpets...


01:03:21.583 --> 01:03:22.958
Tables, chairs...


01:03:23.250 --> 01:03:24.292
All in the fire.


01:03:24.917 --> 01:03:28.125
It was exciting. You get caught up in it.


01:03:30.083 --> 01:03:33.250
We were about to burn our clothes when the police arrived.


01:03:33.500 --> 01:03:34.958
Someone snapped a photo.


01:03:36.667 --> 01:03:39.917
Bizarrely, it's that photo that stuck in people's minds.


01:03:40.625 --> 01:03:43.292
Me, half-naked, smeared with ash.


01:03:44.792 --> 01:03:46.750
The photo of a little girl as psychopath,


01:03:47.333 --> 01:03:48.708
next to her father,


01:03:49.208 --> 01:03:50.333
the psychopath.


01:03:54.042 --> 01:03:56.500
My empty stare in the photo is terrifying.


01:04:03.667 --> 01:04:05.125
Not bad, huh?


01:04:06.875 --> 01:04:07.833
Cognac?


01:04:07.958 --> 01:04:10.417
- Love one.
- Same glass okay?


01:04:13.042 --> 01:04:14.125
Cognac anyone?


01:04:14.208 --> 01:04:15.833
- Me, please.
- Whiskey.


01:04:15.917 --> 01:04:17.750
- Champagne, please.
- I'm out.


01:04:17.833 --> 01:04:20.292
So, one whiskey and one cognac.


01:04:20.792 --> 01:04:21.833
Are you aware


01:04:22.250 --> 01:04:24.500
how mean you were to me at dinner?


01:04:24.583 --> 01:04:25.792
Yes, I am.


01:04:25.875 --> 01:04:27.042
You're cruel


01:04:27.208 --> 01:04:29.708
when you find anything or anyone unpleasant.


01:04:30.125 --> 01:04:31.625
I'm on the list, apparently.


01:04:31.708 --> 01:04:34.833
Neither of us is drunk enough for this conversation.


01:04:35.042 --> 01:04:36.167
Okay?


01:04:48.125 --> 01:04:49.583
- Irène!
- Irène!


01:04:49.667 --> 01:04:50.792
What's happened?


01:04:50.875 --> 01:04:52.208
Can you hear me?


01:04:52.500 --> 01:04:53.958
I don't believe it!


01:04:54.333 --> 01:04:55.667
You better believe it!


01:05:15.083 --> 01:05:16.042
What?


01:05:18.250 --> 01:05:19.500
Go see...


01:05:20.125 --> 01:05:21.375
Your father.


01:05:30.125 --> 01:05:31.750
She's had a major stroke.


01:05:32.375 --> 01:05:36.708
We alleviated the pressure on her brain but she remains unresponsive.


01:05:37.792 --> 01:05:39.542
Unresponsive. meaning?


01:05:40.417 --> 01:05:41.833
She is comatose.


01:05:43.042 --> 01:05:44.167
How long for?


01:05:45.083 --> 01:05:47.417
Sorry, there's no telling.


01:05:47.500 --> 01:05:50.167
- I mean, she's stable...
- This is real?


01:05:51.417 --> 01:05:52.292
Excuse me?


01:05:52.583 --> 01:05:53.833
No. I mean...


01:05:54.833 --> 01:05:59.000
There's no way she's faking it or playing it up?


01:05:59.583 --> 01:06:02.375
You're medically certain this is for real?


01:06:05.208 --> 01:06:08.042
I'm sorry, but yes it's for real.


01:06:08.125 --> 01:06:12.917
In fact, there's a strong probability
your mother will not wake up.


01:06:14.500 --> 01:06:17.250
But as I say, she's stable right now.


01:06:18.000 --> 01:06:20.208
I suggest you get some rest.


01:06:20.500 --> 01:06:22.833
There's nothing you can do here now.


01:06:23.667 --> 01:06:26.417
We'll call you if there's any news.


01:06:32.708 --> 01:06:34.375
Goodbye and thank you.


01:06:34.458 --> 01:06:35.833
Be strong.


01:06:47.958 --> 01:06:49.042
Well?


01:06:50.125 --> 01:06:51.250
It's not good.


01:06:51.667 --> 01:06:53.667
Do you mind sleeping in the guest room?


01:06:54.583 --> 01:06:55.500
No.


01:06:55.833 --> 01:06:57.292
You're sleeping with me.


01:07:03.875 --> 01:07:05.833
Did you see Richard with Hélène?


01:07:06.125 --> 01:07:07.000
I did.


01:07:07.250 --> 01:07:09.708
Telling the same old stories.


01:07:09.792 --> 01:07:11.833
And she seemed amused by them all.


01:07:12.167 --> 01:07:14.333
You'll wind up being good friends.


01:07:15.000 --> 01:07:16.417
No doubt.


01:07:16.500 --> 01:07:19.333
I'll go over for dinner, just the three of us.


01:07:19.750 --> 01:07:22.417
I picture myself at their door with a box of macaroons.


01:07:22.500 --> 01:07:24.500
It makes me want to puke!


01:07:50.792 --> 01:07:52.583
You remember in Cassis?


01:07:53.542 --> 01:07:55.167
We tried.


01:07:59.875 --> 01:08:02.208
It was hopeless. we couldn't stop laughing.


01:08:28.375 --> 01:08:30.042
What are you doing?


01:08:30.125 --> 01:08:33.042
Anna's gone to the office.
I was trying to cheer you up.


01:08:33.167 --> 01:08:35.958
Oddly, your stupidity was what first attracted me.


01:08:37.292 --> 01:08:38.958
Sorry if I misjudged.


01:08:39.042 --> 01:08:40.875
I can't do this anymore. We have to stop.


01:08:42.000 --> 01:08:43.833
You were great and everything.


01:08:43.917 --> 01:08:45.208
We'll stay friends but...


01:08:46.333 --> 01:08:47.500
Are you kidding?


01:08:47.833 --> 01:08:51.167
This whole ridiculous situation is unbearable, right?


01:08:52.042 --> 01:08:52.917
Don't you think?


01:08:53.250 --> 01:08:54.042
No.


01:09:01.542 --> 01:09:02.958
Your breasts are bigger.


01:09:03.250 --> 01:09:04.625
Not that I'm aware of.


01:09:04.708 --> 01:09:06.000
I'm telling you.


01:09:10.292 --> 01:09:12.958
Say you don't want me anymore and we're done.


01:09:13.583 --> 01:09:14.958
It's not that simple.


01:09:16.292 --> 01:09:17.583
But if you like...


01:09:18.208 --> 01:09:21.292
I don't want this anymore, this situation, the lies.


01:09:22.458 --> 01:09:24.208
You dodged my question.


01:09:26.042 --> 01:09:26.917
Sorry.


01:09:27.167 --> 01:09:28.750
I don't want to fuck you anymore.


01:09:29.125 --> 01:09:30.667
Was that the question?


01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:38.292
I won't see him.


01:09:38.583 --> 01:09:40.083
I'm not superstitious.


01:09:40.167 --> 01:09:42.875
I couldn't care less about death-bed requests.


01:09:43.250 --> 01:09:47.250
If you hope to keep manipulating me with this abject stunt...


01:09:48.542 --> 01:09:51.458
Ever since you gave up on basic morality,


01:09:51.542 --> 01:09:54.417
acting out like a spoiled teenager,


01:09:54.542 --> 01:09:56.708
you never gave a shit what I thought.


01:09:57.000 --> 01:09:58.458
How much it hurt me.


01:10:00.750 --> 01:10:02.917
This aneurysm thing is just treachery.


01:10:03.750 --> 01:10:05.000
Disgusting.


01:10:07.208 --> 01:10:10.250
Like this salad, with its shitty olives.


01:10:14.625 --> 01:10:17.417
You can't stay mad at me till the end.


01:10:32.042 --> 01:10:34.792
Sure, the news channel works fine.


01:10:34.917 --> 01:10:36.625
She's in v-tach.


01:10:36.708 --> 01:10:38.208
What's going on?


01:10:40.458 --> 01:10:42.292
What's that beep?


01:10:42.375 --> 01:10:43.042
Ma'am. please.


01:10:43.125 --> 01:10:44.583
Cardiac arrest!


01:10:48.333 --> 01:10:50.417
20 mg of GTN.


01:10:50.583 --> 01:10:52.542
No change. Up it to 40!


01:10:53.625 --> 01:10:55.083
Still no change.


01:10:55.792 --> 01:10:57.000
We're losing her.


01:11:48.125 --> 01:11:49.500
What are you doing?


01:13:03.375 --> 01:13:06.083
I'm looking for a spot with some significance.


01:13:07.667 --> 01:13:10.083
It's not like there'll be a sign that says,


01:13:10.333 --> 01:13:12.000
"Dispose of mother here."


01:13:12.083 --> 01:13:12.875
His pacifier.


01:13:12.958 --> 01:13:16.417
We had a picnic there once, that hollow there.


01:13:17.750 --> 01:13:19.708
I remember only too well.


01:13:21.042 --> 01:13:23.583
Her chicken salad gave me horrific gas.


01:13:23.667 --> 01:13:24.792
You forgot it?


01:13:26.542 --> 01:13:29.042
How can you be such an idiot?


01:13:29.500 --> 01:13:31.333
Three times I reminded you.


01:13:31.542 --> 01:13:34.292
At home and in the car. You enjoy this?


01:13:34.542 --> 01:13:36.250
See how she talks to him?


01:13:36.667 --> 01:13:38.750
Give up the Xbox, moron!


01:13:38.792 --> 01:13:39.708
Stop it.


01:13:39.792 --> 01:13:42.208
Stop it? Stop what?


01:13:42.750 --> 01:13:44.083
I'm embarrassing you?


01:13:44.875 --> 01:13:46.667
All you deserve, asshole!


01:13:52.708 --> 01:13:53.917
Baby blues.


01:13:55.333 --> 01:13:58.458
I hope my boy doesn't inherit her temperament.


01:13:58.917 --> 01:13:59.917
Vincent,


01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:03.500
he's cute but he's not your son. You know that, right?


01:14:03.958 --> 01:14:04.833
Found it.


01:14:06.083 --> 01:14:07.208
Josie!


01:14:07.708 --> 01:14:09.000
Are you listening?


01:14:09.250 --> 01:14:10.125
What's up?


01:14:10.208 --> 01:14:11.500
He's not your son.


01:14:12.583 --> 01:14:14.250
Look at his skin.


01:14:15.083 --> 01:14:17.583
It's two tones darker than yours or Josie's.


01:14:18.458 --> 01:14:20.125
Don't you see?


01:14:20.625 --> 01:14:23.750
- Whose is he, if he's not mine?
- He's his father's!


01:14:24.250 --> 01:14:25.625
His father's not you.


01:14:25.792 --> 01:14:27.917
Sorry, but you're being made a fool of.


01:14:30.042 --> 01:14:32.042
Don't lay a finger on me.


01:14:34.417 --> 01:14:35.375
Cunt!


01:14:35.458 --> 01:14:36.792
What? Say that again.


01:14:37.167 --> 01:14:37.583
Cunt!


01:14:37.667 --> 01:14:39.500
- What?
- Cunt!


01:14:40.958 --> 01:14:42.125
Vincent


01:14:45.792 --> 01:14:46.833
Stop!


01:14:46.917 --> 01:14:48.667
I know why you're angry.


01:14:48.875 --> 01:14:50.333
Leave me alone.


01:14:52.292 --> 01:14:53.750
So what now?


01:14:58.208 --> 01:15:00.250
Okay, this'll have to do.


01:15:02.542 --> 01:15:04.458
The wind's picking up.


01:15:29.667 --> 01:15:31.625
Sorry to bother you. I saw your shutters open.


01:15:31.708 --> 01:15:33.167
Come in.


01:15:34.250 --> 01:15:36.542
Sorry if I'm disturbing you...


01:15:36.625 --> 01:15:37.833
You're not.


01:15:37.917 --> 01:15:40.458
With your shutters open and a storm brewing,


01:15:40.542 --> 01:15:42.417
your windows'll shatter.


01:15:42.500 --> 01:15:43.917
That would be bad timing.


01:15:44.000 --> 01:15:46.000
The wind can do serious damage.


01:15:46.083 --> 01:15:47.083
I know.


01:15:47.167 --> 01:15:49.667
You weren't here in '99. The end of the world.


01:15:49.750 --> 01:15:52.375
I believe it. You need a hand?


01:15:53.000 --> 01:15:54.583
Perhaps, yes. Thanks.


01:15:55.208 --> 01:15:57.458
I never counted. but there must be


01:15:57.542 --> 01:15:59.917
something like 20 windows in this house.


01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:02.333
It's a westerly, so let's start there.


01:16:02.417 --> 01:16:03.667
In the kitchen.


01:16:32.958 --> 01:16:34.042
You're cold?


01:16:34.583 --> 01:16:35.750
A little.


01:16:39.708 --> 01:16:41.250
Next window perhaps?


01:16:44.208 --> 01:16:45.292
Okay.


01:16:50.708 --> 01:16:52.250
I wasn't expecting anyone.


01:17:00.167 --> 01:17:01.875
Looks like a Grumman Wildcat.


01:17:02.583 --> 01:17:03.625
I don't know.


01:17:04.583 --> 01:17:06.292
I'd love to restore one.


01:17:07.625 --> 01:17:09.250
And fly it to New York.


01:17:10.458 --> 01:17:11.625
You're a pilot?


01:17:12.667 --> 01:17:13.583
No.


01:17:14.292 --> 01:17:15.542
You've got to have a dream.


01:17:22.958 --> 01:17:24.458
Let's start with that one.


01:18:06.833 --> 01:18:07.792
Sorry.


01:18:28.917 --> 01:18:31.375
The Summoning scene needs to come later.


01:18:31.458 --> 01:18:34.292
- No. this is...
- Kurt, we have no time to argue.


01:18:34.500 --> 01:18:36.292
The player encounters Kira


01:18:36.375 --> 01:18:38.042
in her sweet, schoolteacher persona


01:18:38.125 --> 01:18:40.125
before her Dark Rebirth.


01:18:40.208 --> 01:18:42.208
- Or there's no boner moment!
- Right.


01:18:45.417 --> 01:18:46.500
- Michèle.
- Yes?


01:18:46.583 --> 01:18:47.792
Got a minute?


01:18:48.875 --> 01:18:49.917
Yeah.


01:18:52.083 --> 01:18:54.542
I found something on Kurt's private server.


01:18:55.292 --> 01:18:57.792
It looks like he's into crushing.


01:18:59.792 --> 01:19:01.083
What's "crushing" ?


01:19:01.250 --> 01:19:03.542
What it sounds like. Crush-sh.


01:19:04.042 --> 01:19:05.417
Enjoy.


01:19:11.750 --> 01:19:14.208
Twisted, but hardly a smoking gun.


01:19:14.750 --> 01:19:16.167
I guess not.


01:19:24.542 --> 01:19:26.208
Good work. Keep on it.


01:20:04.417 --> 01:20:05.458
Ash girl.


01:20:26.000 --> 01:20:27.792
Deliciously nasty.


01:20:28.750 --> 01:20:30.292
Deliciously nasty.


01:20:40.708 --> 01:20:41.750
You're here?


01:20:47.583 --> 01:20:48.500
You're mad?


01:20:48.583 --> 01:20:50.125
I'm mostly curious.


01:20:51.750 --> 01:20:52.917
I guess I should explain.


01:20:57.875 --> 01:20:59.875
I was never going to show it to anyone.


01:21:00.917 --> 01:21:02.708
Philippe Kwan ripped it off my computer


01:21:02.792 --> 01:21:04.375
and sent it out.


01:21:04.458 --> 01:21:05.958
But you created it?


01:21:08.250 --> 01:21:09.000
Yes.


01:21:09.083 --> 01:21:09.875
Why?


01:21:11.208 --> 01:21:13.750
At first, as a game idea


01:21:13.833 --> 01:21:15.250
based on true crime photos.


01:21:15.792 --> 01:21:17.083
Then it got weird.


01:21:18.250 --> 01:21:19.667
Nobody would've seen it


01:21:19.750 --> 01:21:21.333
if that asshole Kwan hadn't...


01:21:21.875 --> 01:21:23.625
If I'm fired, he deserves it too.


01:21:26.625 --> 01:21:27.792
Take out your dick.


01:21:31.208 --> 01:21:32.000
Pardon me?


01:21:32.375 --> 01:21:34.542
Show me your dick and I might not fire you.


01:21:52.300 --> 01:21:54.300
It's pretty.


01:21:54.475 --> 01:21:56.475
Manon.


01:21:57.475 --> 01:21:59.475
You look circumcised.


01:22:03.000 --> 01:22:04.458
I still get the 10 grand?


01:22:06.083 --> 01:22:07.083
That's a no.


01:22:07.750 --> 01:22:09.667
And delete all that.


01:22:32.958 --> 01:22:34.583
Fantastic!


01:24:06.625 --> 01:24:08.958
Get out!


01:24:09.625 --> 01:24:11.042
Get out!


01:24:11.167 --> 01:24:12.583
Get out of here!


01:24:14.750 --> 01:24:16.250
Get out!


01:25:22.875 --> 01:25:24.958
A wave of enthusiasm in Spain.


01:25:25.042 --> 01:25:29.042
Pope Francis will join crowds of pilgrims walking barefoot


01:25:29.125 --> 01:25:32.292
on the road to Santiago de Compostela.


01:25:32.625 --> 01:25:33.500
In France,


01:25:33.583 --> 01:25:36.417
Georges Leblanc stays in prison, unsurprisingly.


01:25:36.500 --> 01:25:38.583
The serial killer failed


01:25:38.667 --> 01:25:41.917
in his latest application for parole.


01:25:42.083 --> 01:25:45.250
Georges Leblanc is 76 years old.


01:25:45.333 --> 01:25:48.583
He must wait ten years to apply again.


01:25:48.750 --> 01:25:50.625
His lawyers announced he...


01:25:57.500 --> 01:25:59.708
Fuck you, fuck you!


01:26:37.333 --> 01:26:41.083
I'm Michèle Leblanc. I called yesterday.


01:26:42.042 --> 01:26:42.958
Right.


01:26:43.458 --> 01:26:45.458
Wait there for someone to come get you.


01:26:45.792 --> 01:26:46.667
Thank you.


01:26:58.833 --> 01:26:59.792
Ms. Leblanc?


01:27:01.583 --> 01:27:03.542
- I'm the Assistant Warden.
- Hi.


01:27:03.750 --> 01:27:06.333
- A coffee or something?
- No, thanks.


01:27:06.417 --> 01:27:10.125
Can we talk in my office if you don't mind? This way...


01:27:10.458 --> 01:27:12.917
I'm here to spit in my father's face.


01:27:13.000 --> 01:27:14.875
I can't guarantee it's a metaphor.


01:27:14.958 --> 01:27:16.208
People have all kinds of reasons.


01:27:19.042 --> 01:27:22.417
I came because I gave the bastard too much power over me.


01:27:22.500 --> 01:27:25.708
My whole life fleeing him, fearing him.


01:27:27.292 --> 01:27:28.583
What a waste!


01:27:28.917 --> 01:27:30.083
Ms. Leblanc...


01:27:30.667 --> 01:27:32.208
Your father is dead.


01:27:35.167 --> 01:27:36.542
Shortly before 8 AM,


01:27:36.625 --> 01:27:39.125
we found him deceased in his cell.


01:27:40.167 --> 01:27:41.208
How?


01:27:42.167 --> 01:27:43.500
There'll be an investigation,


01:27:43.583 --> 01:27:47.083
but he appears to have hanged himself with a sheet.


01:27:57.625 --> 01:27:59.333
When did this happen?


01:28:00.708 --> 01:28:04.750
We only know it must have been between 7pm and 7am.


01:28:12.333 --> 01:28:15.875
At what time was my father notified that I was coming today?


01:28:19.708 --> 01:28:21.667
Shortly before 7pm.


01:28:24.375 --> 01:28:26.083
Your mother requested cremation,


01:28:26.167 --> 01:28:28.708
with a vault for his ashes next to hers.


01:28:28.792 --> 01:28:32.333
She won't be there, even if her plaque's next to his.


01:28:48.583 --> 01:28:51.083
I had a list of things to say to him.


01:28:51.167 --> 01:28:52.833
Nine bullet points.


01:28:58.375 --> 01:29:00.375
I killed you by coming here.


01:29:24.167 --> 01:29:24.875
Hello?


01:29:24.958 --> 01:29:27.042
Emilie Fontaine, reporter at Le Parisien.


01:29:27.125 --> 01:29:31.583
I was wondering if you'd like to comment on your father's passing.


01:29:31.667 --> 01:29:33.500
How did you get this number?


01:29:34.083 --> 01:29:35.875
I realize it's an awkward time.


01:29:35.958 --> 01:29:37.958
It's an opportunity for you...


01:29:46.375 --> 01:29:47.125
Hello?


01:29:47.875 --> 01:29:49.000
Ms. Leblanc?


01:29:50.167 --> 01:29:51.208
Ms. Leblanc?


01:29:51.917 --> 01:29:53.375
Are you feeling anger?


01:29:54.125 --> 01:29:55.375
Grief?


01:29:55.667 --> 01:29:57.542
Relief perhaps?


01:30:12.250 --> 01:30:15.000
Anna's voicemail. I can't take your...


01:30:18.917 --> 01:30:21.125
This is Richard. Leave me a message.


01:30:59.583 --> 01:31:00.875
How are you feeling?


01:31:02.458 --> 01:31:03.750
How am I feeling?


01:31:04.083 --> 01:31:06.333
Are you dizzy? Head spinning?


01:31:06.417 --> 01:31:08.750
- No. I'm fine, I think.
- Ok.


01:31:09.000 --> 01:31:10.333
Except my leg.


01:31:12.875 --> 01:31:15.167
Don't bother. It's jammed.


01:31:15.500 --> 01:31:17.667
Unbuckle and I'll help you out.


01:31:43.833 --> 01:31:45.375
You should let me look at it.


01:31:45.833 --> 01:31:47.292
I played soccer.


01:31:48.708 --> 01:31:50.125
Great, so what?


01:31:50.667 --> 01:31:53.667
I mean, I know a bit about leg injuries.


01:31:54.208 --> 01:31:57.125
As a teen, I tore my anterior cruciate ligament.


01:31:57.458 --> 01:31:58.458
Okay?


01:31:59.500 --> 01:32:01.208
One year of rehab.


01:32:03.333 --> 01:32:07.292
Alright, I'd better disinfect it now.


01:32:12.000 --> 01:32:13.292
A nasty sprain.


01:32:13.375 --> 01:32:14.792
It needs treatment.


01:32:28.792 --> 01:32:30.250
So, how was it?


01:32:45.542 --> 01:32:47.458
Was it good? How was it?


01:32:57.708 --> 01:32:59.667
Answer me. Did you enjoy it?


01:33:11.375 --> 01:33:13.208
Why did you do it?


01:33:19.167 --> 01:33:20.667
It was necessary.


01:33:41.708 --> 01:33:44.333
- Have a good day, ma'am.
- Thanks. goodbye.


01:34:02.125 --> 01:34:04.333
Stop it, Michèle. You can't do this.


01:34:05.000 --> 01:34:06.125
What can't I do?


01:34:06.375 --> 01:34:08.542
Walking in without ringing the bell.


01:34:08.750 --> 01:34:11.333
I have a key, Ralf. Why ring the bell?


01:34:11.708 --> 01:34:13.500
Ignore me, I won't be long.


01:34:13.583 --> 01:34:15.375
It's not about how long.


01:34:15.458 --> 01:34:17.875
- Don't be unpleasant.
- You have to go immediately.


01:34:17.958 --> 01:34:19.917
I own this apartment!


01:34:20.117 --> 01:34:22.117
Yes, well I will be going...


01:34:23.142 --> 01:34:25.142
This is not the time.


01:34:26.142 --> 01:34:28.142
Anyway I put on sale, that's why I'm here.


01:34:32.167 --> 01:34:34.000
I saw your father passed away.


01:34:35.083 --> 01:34:37.000
One less bastard in the world.


01:34:39.792 --> 01:34:42.083
You should start packing your bags.


01:34:44.042 --> 01:34:46.833
I saw all the shows on TV about you and your dad.


01:34:47.125 --> 01:34:49.000
When you murdered all those people.


01:34:55.542 --> 01:34:58.000
I saw all the corpses, all the dead children.


01:35:03.375 --> 01:35:06.708
The bastard's dead now, and at least I fucked his wife.


01:35:16.958 --> 01:35:17.708
Hello?


01:35:17.792 --> 01:35:18.583
It's Robert.


01:35:18.667 --> 01:35:21.667
Anna's gone to her London meeting. My afternoon's free.


01:35:21.917 --> 01:35:22.917
Robert.


01:35:23.333 --> 01:35:24.208
I was going to call.


01:35:24.292 --> 01:35:26.875
I sprained my knee. It's in a brace.


01:35:27.250 --> 01:35:28.667
I can hardly walk.


01:35:29.042 --> 01:35:31.500
So? We're not going skiing.


01:35:55.167 --> 01:35:56.292
You were fabulous.


01:35:56.375 --> 01:35:58.417
Where'd you get the idea of playing dead?


01:35:59.417 --> 01:36:01.125
Anyway. you got what you wanted.


01:36:02.125 --> 01:36:03.708
See, I'm as good as my word.


01:36:03.875 --> 01:36:05.167
Now that...


01:36:05.667 --> 01:36:08.417
It was a very peculiar sensation.


01:36:10.250 --> 01:36:11.833
So we can still be friends.


01:36:14.625 --> 01:36:16.333
You know what I mean by "friends"?


01:36:17.500 --> 01:36:18.625
No more fucking.


01:36:27.083 --> 01:36:28.125
Vincent


01:36:33.500 --> 01:36:34.708
What are you doing here?


01:36:37.833 --> 01:36:39.500
Josie kicked me out.


01:36:40.250 --> 01:36:41.500
What happened?


01:36:42.500 --> 01:36:43.708
I don't know.


01:36:44.958 --> 01:36:46.417
So think about it.


01:36:47.000 --> 01:36:49.167
There must be a reason, however demented.


01:36:49.250 --> 01:36:50.583
There's a reason.


01:36:51.167 --> 01:36:52.458
I lost my job.


01:36:53.083 --> 01:36:53.875
Lost?


01:36:54.542 --> 01:36:55.792
I resigned.


01:36:55.833 --> 01:36:57.875
-You resigned? -l had to.


01:36:58.042 --> 01:36:59.458
My car broke down.


01:37:00.375 --> 01:37:02.875
You resigned because your car broke down?


01:37:02.958 --> 01:37:06.083
It's one hour there, one hour back, from the house.


01:37:06.167 --> 01:37:07.542
That's unhealthy.


01:37:08.708 --> 01:37:12.000
I saw a thing on TV about air quality in the subway.


01:37:15.333 --> 01:37:16.875
You brought him here?


01:37:20.000 --> 01:37:22.417
-l had no choice. -No choice?


01:37:24.292 --> 01:37:26.625
Josie threatened to go to America.


01:37:27.375 --> 01:37:28.542
And take Lucien along.


01:37:28.625 --> 01:37:31.917
I can't believe I'm defending her


01:37:32.000 --> 01:37:34.208
but she has a right to be mad at you.


01:37:34.625 --> 01:37:38.250
You have responsibilities, an apartment, and you quit your job?


01:37:38.333 --> 01:37:40.458
You say it exactly like her.


01:37:40.542 --> 01:37:43.125
My car broke down. That's not my fault!


01:37:43.208 --> 01:37:45.625
You have to give that baby back right now.


01:37:45.708 --> 01:37:48.292
You're not married. It could be seen as kidnapping.


01:37:48.500 --> 01:37:49.958
Kidnapping? He's my son!


01:37:51.833 --> 01:37:52.542
My son!


01:37:52.625 --> 01:37:53.958
Alright, he's your son.


01:37:54.042 --> 01:37:55.250
No, not alright.


01:37:58.458 --> 01:37:59.917
Who could that be?


01:38:06.167 --> 01:38:07.042
Where is he?


01:38:07.125 --> 01:38:08.583
- Who?
- My baby!


01:38:09.625 --> 01:38:11.750
- Where is he?
- Upstairs.


01:38:13.042 --> 01:38:15.375
My baby! What did you do to him?


01:38:15.750 --> 01:38:16.667
What did I do to him?


01:38:16.750 --> 01:38:19.083
I wouldn't trust you with a hamster!


01:38:19.500 --> 01:38:21.583
Let go! Let go of me!


01:38:21.667 --> 01:38:22.958
Let go of her.


01:38:23.042 --> 01:38:24.750
Let go of me, dammit!


01:38:24.833 --> 01:38:26.542
Let go of her!


01:38:26.625 --> 01:38:27.958
Let go of me!


01:38:30.833 --> 01:38:31.875
Vincent!


01:38:32.167 --> 01:38:33.292
What?


01:38:36.792 --> 01:38:38.542
He's my baby, get it?


01:38:40.458 --> 01:38:41.917
My child!


01:38:54.250 --> 01:38:56.833
It was always about the baby for you.


01:38:58.083 --> 01:39:00.000
You were in it for his sake.


01:39:02.208 --> 01:39:03.917
I could be a good father.


01:39:04.958 --> 01:39:06.125
I know it.


01:39:12.958 --> 01:39:13.917
These?


01:39:15.958 --> 01:39:17.625
Sure, but unsalted ones.


01:39:20.417 --> 01:39:21.875
Hi, Vincent.


01:39:22.583 --> 01:39:23.875
- Okay?
- And you?


01:39:23.917 --> 01:39:26.750
Buy Bonne Vie. They're made in Florange.


01:39:32.958 --> 01:39:34.208
Evening, Michèle.


01:39:35.708 --> 01:39:37.000
How's your knee?


01:39:37.667 --> 01:39:38.667
And you? Your hand?


01:39:40.333 --> 01:39:41.375
Patrick said Bonne Vie unsalted chips


01:39:41.458 --> 01:39:43.917
are made in Florange.


01:39:45.917 --> 01:39:48.625
Rebecca's on a trip and left tons of lasagna.


01:39:48.917 --> 01:39:50.917
I'll never be able to finish it.


01:39:52.000 --> 01:39:53.917
I got this to go with it.


01:39:55.417 --> 01:39:56.750
Sounds good to me.


01:40:01.292 --> 01:40:02.917
Yes. sure.


01:40:04.500 --> 01:40:05.833
No, thanks.


01:40:08.583 --> 01:40:10.542
Where did Rebecca and her parents go?


01:40:11.042 --> 01:40:13.583
To see the Pope in Santiago de Compostela.


01:40:14.625 --> 01:40:16.500
Driving and on foot at the end.


01:40:16.583 --> 01:40:19.250
I saw he'll be saying mass in the cathedral.


01:40:20.375 --> 01:40:21.250
The Pope.


01:40:21.667 --> 01:40:25.208
I have a hard time imagining the guy barefoot.


01:40:25.583 --> 01:40:29.250
It's so weird to think he's a real person, like with feet.


01:40:33.625 --> 01:40:35.458
Go easy, sweetheart.


01:40:48.417 --> 01:40:49.458
He's out.


01:40:50.375 --> 01:40:52.250
Eyes bigger than his belly.


01:40:53.625 --> 01:40:54.875
Thank you.


01:41:27.125 --> 01:41:28.792
The floor's warm.


01:41:30.500 --> 01:41:34.000
It's a wood boiler. I installed it myself.


01:41:35.833 --> 01:41:37.208
Sounds like a job.


01:41:38.042 --> 01:41:39.458
Yes.


01:41:40.417 --> 01:41:42.500
Works by inverted flame combustion.


01:41:44.417 --> 01:41:46.500
Inverted flame combustion?


01:41:47.208 --> 01:41:50.125
- Sounds like you just made it up.
- No.


01:41:50.625 --> 01:41:52.042
I'm not making anything up.


01:42:01.500 --> 01:42:02.750
It's in the basement.


01:42:08.708 --> 01:42:10.125
I can imagine.


01:42:14.083 --> 01:42:15.500
You want to see it?


01:42:24.875 --> 01:42:25.792
Ok.


01:43:04.750 --> 01:43:05.875
There we are.


01:43:08.292 --> 01:43:10.667
All noise is muffled by the door.


01:43:22.625 --> 01:43:24.500
-Vincent's upstairs. -Yes, he is.


01:43:37.750 --> 01:43:38.708
Do it.


01:43:44.875 --> 01:43:46.917
It doesn't work like that.


01:43:47.667 --> 01:43:48.792
Not for me.


01:43:50.000 --> 01:43:51.417
It has to be like before.


01:44:58.708 --> 01:44:59.958
Let's go.


01:45:14.208 --> 01:45:15.667
Thank you for dinner.


01:45:15.750 --> 01:45:16.625
Anytime.


01:45:48.958 --> 01:45:49.667
Kurt.


01:45:51.333 --> 01:45:52.500
Bravo.


01:45:56.667 --> 01:45:59.167
Anna, I have an idea.


01:45:59.500 --> 01:46:01.125
The party for the game launch.


01:46:01.208 --> 01:46:03.083
we could ask Vincent to organize it.


01:46:03.417 --> 01:46:04.500
Good idea.


01:46:04.667 --> 01:46:08.625
I know I was always against throwing work Vincent's way but...


01:46:11.417 --> 01:46:12.583
What's wrong?


01:46:16.708 --> 01:46:18.333
Robert's fucking someone.


01:46:22.708 --> 01:46:23.958
Are you sure?


01:46:27.667 --> 01:46:29.500
I recognized the scent


01:46:29.708 --> 01:46:32.708
of that stupid body wash they use in hotels


01:46:32.792 --> 01:46:34.542
trying to be classy.


01:46:34.917 --> 01:46:36.667
We don't have that at home.


01:46:39.875 --> 01:46:41.542
That's your only evidence?


01:46:45.333 --> 01:46:47.292
I smelled his underwear.


01:46:51.375 --> 01:46:54.875
I waited all day for him to take off his shorts.


01:46:55.333 --> 01:46:59.333
When he did at last, I pounced on them. And sniffed.


01:47:01.292 --> 01:47:02.917
I felt ashamed beyond words.


01:47:04.208 --> 01:47:08.333
Shame isn't a strong enough emotion to stop us doing anything at all.


01:47:09.917 --> 01:47:11.083
Believe me.


01:47:31.458 --> 01:47:32.917
You're becoming a regular.


01:47:33.000 --> 01:47:34.458
Looks like it.


01:47:34.542 --> 01:47:36.833
- Your wife?
- Couldn't make it.


01:47:38.708 --> 01:47:39.833
What do you mean, "Ah''?


01:47:40.083 --> 01:47:42.750
We should've come together. Carpooling is hip.


01:47:43.500 --> 01:47:45.458
How are you?


01:47:45.833 --> 01:47:49.458
Fauchon made this up for us.
Taste that. it's awesome.


01:47:49.917 --> 01:47:51.792
- Hi.
- Hi.


01:47:51.875 --> 01:47:52.792
Right this way.


01:47:53.458 --> 01:47:54.667
You're maitre d' tonight?


01:47:54.750 --> 01:47:58.208
Mom put me in charge of the party.


01:47:58.542 --> 01:47:59.667
Evening.


01:48:00.708 --> 01:48:02.333
- How are you?
- Fine.


01:48:03.250 --> 01:48:04.625
- Good evening.
- Good evening.


01:48:04.708 --> 01:48:06.500
- How are you?
- Good.


01:48:07.542 --> 01:48:09.875
Sorry, lipstick on your cheek.


01:48:10.792 --> 01:48:12.500
Welcome to my home.


01:48:13.375 --> 01:48:14.625
Want to give it a try?


01:48:15.042 --> 01:48:16.667
No, thanks, I'm no gamer.


01:48:16.708 --> 01:48:17.333
Really?


01:48:17.417 --> 01:48:19.875
- I'd love a go. Show me?
- Ok.


01:48:23.042 --> 01:48:24.542
- Good evening.
- Good evening.


01:48:24.875 --> 01:48:26.083
Can I get you a drink?


01:48:26.167 --> 01:48:28.042
- Champagne?
- Red wine, please.


01:48:28.125 --> 01:48:29.625
I'll switch to red, too.


01:48:29.708 --> 01:48:32.292
- Champagne for you?
- No, I'm good.


01:48:33.875 --> 01:48:35.250
Bottle of red, please.


01:48:35.458 --> 01:48:37.542
I was told to pour glasses.


01:48:38.083 --> 01:48:39.167
I'm in charge here.


01:48:39.250 --> 01:48:41.125
I was given specific instructions.


01:48:41.292 --> 01:48:42.958
Whiskey here, please.


01:48:50.792 --> 01:48:52.417
Faster, much faster!


01:48:52.500 --> 01:48:54.292
You can press the circle.


01:48:54.583 --> 01:48:56.083
Get him moving now.


01:48:56.167 --> 01:48:57.458
Press there to jump.


01:49:00.375 --> 01:49:02.333
You didn't bring Hélène?


01:49:02.917 --> 01:49:04.375
We've met now.


01:49:05.458 --> 01:49:08.083
I won't lie to you. It's over.


01:49:08.500 --> 01:49:10.083
What happened?


01:49:11.708 --> 01:49:15.500
Laying in bed, I asked her which of my books was her favorite.


01:49:15.958 --> 01:49:18.292
Why'd you do that?


01:49:18.375 --> 01:49:20.042
She said Scent of Poplar.


01:49:20.458 --> 01:49:21.917
Scent of Poplar


01:49:22.375 --> 01:49:24.833
is a novel by one Pierre Casamayou.


01:49:35.833 --> 01:49:38.083
I'd no idea there were two Casamayous.


01:49:38.167 --> 01:49:39.958
Apparently, he's talented.


01:49:42.000 --> 01:49:43.208
Poor Richard.


01:49:43.458 --> 01:49:45.792
Yes, poor Richard.


01:49:59.417 --> 01:50:00.917
So...


01:50:01.375 --> 01:50:05.292
It looks like somehow, despite our best efforts,


01:50:05.625 --> 01:50:08.042
we have a success on our hands.


01:50:09.042 --> 01:50:11.375
All I can say is thank you.


01:50:11.458 --> 01:50:15.000
to your good health and hip hip hooray!


01:50:19.583 --> 01:50:27.167
Michèle! Michèle! Michèle!


01:50:27.250 --> 01:50:28.875
Michèle! Michèle!


01:50:32.458 --> 01:50:34.625
Well...


01:50:34.833 --> 01:50:37.542
I couldn't put it any better.


01:50:39.708 --> 01:50:41.417
Have a great evening!


01:50:45.792 --> 01:50:47.125
Have you met Richard?


01:50:47.250 --> 01:50:50.958
Some time ago, Richard pitched a very interesting idea.


01:50:51.042 --> 01:50:54.875
You two working together could make something fabulous of it.


01:50:55.083 --> 01:50:56.333
I think, at least.


01:50:57.042 --> 01:50:59.333
Talk it over.


01:51:00.500 --> 01:51:02.500
This isn't charity?


01:51:02.583 --> 01:51:06.667
You should know me better than that.


01:51:06.750 --> 01:51:09.000
Go on, tell him your idea.


01:51:10.792 --> 01:51:12.625
So, it's set in a...


01:51:12.750 --> 01:51:14.583
Let me get you a drink.


01:51:19.417 --> 01:51:21.833
We can go whenever you want, darling.


01:51:22.000 --> 01:51:24.625
We'll have more fun in bed than here.


01:51:49.875 --> 01:51:51.875
How about a whiskey, guys?


01:51:53.958 --> 01:51:55.708
Give me a minute, then we can go.


01:51:55.792 --> 01:51:57.417
Whatever you say.


01:52:01.500 --> 01:52:03.875
Two whiskeys and an OJ, please.


01:52:06.333 --> 01:52:07.500
It's going great!


01:52:10.208 --> 01:52:11.417
It's me.


01:52:12.375 --> 01:52:13.458
What's you?


01:52:15.958 --> 01:52:17.958
It's me, sleeping with Robert.


01:52:21.958 --> 01:52:24.208
It's over now, but it was me.


01:52:35.417 --> 01:52:36.500
How long?


01:52:37.042 --> 01:52:38.208
6-8 months.


01:52:45.625 --> 01:52:47.167
I didn't have a clue.


01:52:47.917 --> 01:52:49.292
I know.


01:53:03.458 --> 01:53:04.917
What did you do?


01:53:05.875 --> 01:53:07.542
I stopped lying.


01:53:21.250 --> 01:53:22.583
- See you.
- See you.


01:53:24.750 --> 01:53:26.917
Take my keys. Patrick's driving me home.


01:53:27.000 --> 01:53:29.667
-You're leaving already? -You did wonderfully.


01:53:29.750 --> 01:53:30.792
Relax.


01:53:31.167 --> 01:53:32.083
See you.


01:53:48.583 --> 01:53:50.000
It's twisted.


01:53:52.625 --> 01:53:53.625
- Sorry?
- Twisted.


01:53:53.708 --> 01:53:56.500
Between us, it's sick. Diseased.


01:54:01.125 --> 01:54:04.625
I was in some kind of weird denial but I see clearly now.


01:54:08.083 --> 01:54:09.583
What do you see?


01:54:11.583 --> 01:54:14.417
You don't expect to get away with what you did to me?


01:54:18.917 --> 01:54:21.292
I'll do what I should've done at once.


01:54:22.417 --> 01:54:23.667
What do you mean?


01:54:24.000 --> 01:54:26.958
It's not just about me. There's your wife, too.


01:54:28.792 --> 01:54:30.583
And others, perhaps.


01:54:31.625 --> 01:54:32.708
Who knows.


01:54:34.583 --> 01:54:35.667
What do you mean?


01:54:35.750 --> 01:54:39.458
How many others? That you've done the same thing to?


01:54:44.042 --> 01:54:47.500
I'll go to the police. I'll tell them everything.


01:58:17.792 --> 01:58:19.667
Why?


01:58:40.917 --> 01:58:43.250
It's over.


01:58:52.833 --> 01:58:54.500
It's over.


01:58:57.333 --> 01:58:58.542
It's over.


01:59:08.792 --> 01:59:10.000
Ms. Leblanc?


01:59:20.208 --> 01:59:21.458
-Hello. -Hello.


01:59:30.792 --> 01:59:33.958
What was your relationship with the deceased?


01:59:37.417 --> 01:59:39.000
He was my neighbor.


01:59:39.625 --> 01:59:42.958
Like have-a-cup-of-coffee neighbor?


01:59:43.542 --> 01:59:45.583
Borrow-the-lawnmower neighbor?


01:59:46.292 --> 01:59:49.417
No, I never borrowed his lawnmower.


01:59:49.500 --> 01:59:51.208
But it was...


01:59:52.042 --> 01:59:54.417
Yes, that kind of neighbor.


01:59:54.500 --> 01:59:56.167
Until maybe...


01:59:58.167 --> 01:59:59.083
recently.


01:59:59.500 --> 02:00:01.750
When he attended this party with you?


02:00:03.042 --> 02:00:03.750
Yes.


02:00:04.333 --> 02:00:07.083
That's when your relationship became


02:00:07.792 --> 02:00:09.667
more personal?


02:00:13.542 --> 02:00:15.250
Yes. I mean...


02:00:17.000 --> 02:00:18.958
It was heading in that direction.


02:00:21.208 --> 02:00:24.000
When this man appeared in your house, masked,


02:00:24.792 --> 02:00:29.417
you never suspected for a moment it might be your neighbor?


02:00:33.208 --> 02:00:35.583
Who could imagine such a thing?


02:00:54.000 --> 02:00:56.000
- The color okay for you?
- Just fine.


02:00:56.208 --> 02:00:57.333
It's perfect.


02:01:10.542 --> 02:01:12.750
Careful, the statues are fragile.


02:01:12.792 --> 02:01:13.917
Rebecca!


02:01:16.792 --> 02:01:18.000
Hi.


02:01:19.417 --> 02:01:21.000
You found a buyer?


02:01:21.208 --> 02:01:23.333
I took a bit of a hit, but not too bad.


02:01:23.417 --> 02:01:25.417
The realtor did a great job.


02:01:25.750 --> 02:01:27.917
I'll give you his details. If ever you...


02:01:28.000 --> 02:01:30.042
I'm not going anywhere.


02:01:34.625 --> 02:01:36.208
Stuff piles up.


02:01:37.583 --> 02:01:39.292
I wanted you to know...


02:01:40.292 --> 02:01:41.667
I'm ...


02:01:43.042 --> 02:01:45.750
I'm very sorry for all you've been through.


02:01:47.875 --> 02:01:49.667
Fortunately, I have faith.


02:01:50.417 --> 02:01:53.042
What's it for if not to get through tough times?


02:01:54.042 --> 02:01:58.083
Patrick was a good man but he had a tortured soul.


02:02:05.042 --> 02:02:06.958
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.


02:02:09.792 --> 02:02:10.792
Michèle!


02:02:12.458 --> 02:02:15.583
I'm sincerely glad you could give him what he needed.


02:02:15.667 --> 02:02:17.083
For a time, at least.


02:02:35.583 --> 02:02:36.792
Hey there!


02:02:37.542 --> 02:02:39.000
Wow, beautiful!


02:02:39.083 --> 02:02:39.958
Check it out.


02:02:40.250 --> 02:02:41.750
Josie let me choose.


02:02:43.417 --> 02:02:44.542
A convertible.


02:02:44.625 --> 02:02:45.917
He's earned it.


02:02:46.000 --> 02:02:47.167
Hello.


02:02:50.917 --> 02:02:52.250
Let's go.


02:02:54.625 --> 02:02:55.917
Baby!


02:03:01.500 --> 02:03:02.458
Happy?


02:03:03.792 --> 02:03:05.000
Crazy!


02:03:32.417 --> 02:03:33.875
I heard you were here.


02:03:38.833 --> 02:03:40.292
Physically, anyway.


02:03:52.083 --> 02:03:54.292
We're going ahead with Richard's project?


02:03:54.375 --> 02:03:56.625
Let him fool around for a while.


02:03:59.000 --> 02:04:00.583
How's Robert?


02:04:03.208 --> 02:04:05.583
- I kicked him out.
- No.


02:04:06.125 --> 02:04:08.292
Ever since, he's hit the bottle.


02:04:09.292 --> 02:04:10.958
What did you see in him?


02:04:11.583 --> 02:04:13.375
It was just one of those things.


02:04:13.833 --> 02:04:15.000
An opportunity.


02:04:16.083 --> 02:04:17.417
I wanted to get laid.


02:04:20.375 --> 02:04:23.500
That's no excuse. It was shabby.


02:04:25.000 --> 02:04:26.583
Worse than that even.


02:04:37.250 --> 02:04:38.958
Vincent's grown up now.


02:04:40.042 --> 02:04:41.458
It's just the two of us.


02:04:42.958 --> 02:04:45.208
And I'm all alone in that huge house.


02:04:46.292 --> 02:04:47.583
I'm going to sell it.


02:04:48.917 --> 02:04:52.917
I was thinking I could move in with you for a while.

